WEBVTT


00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:45.700
Jessica McDowell, Gnosos Chemicals.


00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:47.600
When do you leave Kuala Lumpur,
Miss McDowell?


00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:50.500
I fly to Taiwan Tuesday,
then back to Düsseldorf.


00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:54.800
Mr. Tabir is very busy this morning.


00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:56.200
I can imagine.


00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:03.200
Seeing as we are waiting


00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:05.700
why don't you practice
your little pitch on me?


00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:09.900
Actually, if it's all the same, I'll just be...


00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:11.800
I know all of my uncle's business.


00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:13.200
He trusts me.


00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:15.100
Begin.


00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:23.500
Well, I'm sure you're aware
that recently your subsidiary


00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:27.900
developed an organic, ester-based lubricant
derived from kernel oil that makes...


00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:29.000
You are American?


00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:33.300
Canadian, actually. I'm from Toronto.


00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.500
A Maple Leaf fan?


00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:36.900
No, not really.


00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:41.100
You must be the only person from Toronto
who's not a hockey fan.


00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:45.200
Oh, I'm a fan.
Dad's from Vancouver so I'm a Canuck.


00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:49.300
Between us, the Maple Leafs suck.
They should never have signed Mark Bell.


00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:53.200
Guy's a liability on and off the ice.
So, who's your team?


00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:55.900
I don't like hockey.


00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:59.600
Unfortunately, Mr. Tabir
has no window this morning.


00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:03.600
He extends an invitation
to a private reception at his residence.


00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:06.100
Well, if that's okay. I don't want to intrude.


00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:08.600
Come to the party.


00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:24.400
Why are we stopping?


00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:27.600
Miss McDowell,


00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:31.400
my uncle believes
trust is something you earn.


00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:35.800
He doesn't trust people
until he knows them very, very well.


00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:40.500
But he trusts you, Hafiz.


00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:44.100
How do you know my name?


00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:51.600
Your car was swept an hour ago.


00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:54.800
Do not get out.
If you get out of this car, I can't protect you.


00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:57.200
- Who are you?
- Let go of my arm.


00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:58.300
- Who are you?
- Now!


00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:02.000
Your uncle's in business
with Abu Domar Khan.


00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:04.600
Khan has made contact
with a terror organization


00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:06.600
via an aid agency in Pakistan.


00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:08.800
They're seeking materials
to build a weapon.


00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:11.300
- That's bullshit.
- We need information about your uncle.


00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:13.900
Contacts. Shipments.


00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:18.800
If you help us, we help you.
If you don't, your brother dies.


00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:22.400
And tomorrow you're sitting
next to your uncle in a cell in Thailand


00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:24.200
and it won't be me asking the questions.


00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:26.400
- No. No, you can't help him.
- We can help him, Hafiz.


00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:29.500
Listen to me,
because I promise you one thing.


00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:32.600
Right now you have no idea
what we can and cannot do.


00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:36.000
You'll get a call at 8:00 a.m.


00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:38.600
You'll be asked if you need a cleaner.


00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:42.100
You want her to come three mornings
per week, do you understand?


00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:47.700
I said, do you understand?


00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:54.300
Tonight I want to take a few minutes
to discuss a great threat to peace,


00:03:55.800 --> 00:04:00.700
and America's determination
to lead the world in confronting that threat.


00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:05.000
The decision has been made to increase
the threat condition designation


00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:07.300
currently classified at Elevated Risk


00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:12.600
to increase that threat condition
designation to the High Risk category.


00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:17.000
9/11 and its aftermath
awakened this nation to danger.


00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:21.300
To the true ambitions
of the global terror network.


00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:24.100
The state police are investigating
an Anthrax scare.


00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:26.200
Threatening letters with a white substance.


00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:34.000
The Nuclear Regulatory Commission


00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:37.100
has placed the nation's nuclear plants
on their highest level of security.


00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:39.200
A terrorist attack is now highly likely.


00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:41.400
What do we know after September 11th?


00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:45.800
We know these terrorist networks
will use any means they can


00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:47.700
to cause maximum death and destruction.


00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:51.000
And we will take whatever action
is necessary


00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:53.800
to defend our freedom and our security.


00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:09.400
America strikes back.
Afghanistan is pounded


00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:11.800
with bombs and missiles
from the air and from sea.


00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:13.400
American-led military attacks


00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:16.100
against targets throughout Afghanistan
continue tonight.


00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:19.100
He couldn't slow down for, like, 400 yards.


00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:20.600
And yet, I'm incredible in bed.


00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:24.300
They are targeting


00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:28.200
both Osama bin Laden's training camps
and Taliban military.


00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:33.100
Listen, Steven and I are not gonna go
on the same plane together.


00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:34.700
We're not even
going to take a train together.


00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:36.000
We took the train to your mom's.


00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:39.300
It only takes one
to fly into a nuclear power plant.


00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:41.000
- One.
- A sarin attack on Disneyworld.


00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:43.800
Yeah, but whatever they're telling us,
we're totally vulnerable.


00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:45.500
I mean, who is protecting us?


00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:48.200
Would you risk taking your kids
to Disneyworld right now?


00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:50.300
- Would you do that?
- Absolutely not.


00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:54.300
I'd be terrified of exposing my children
to what adds up to a clearinghouse


00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:57.000
for crap merchandise
and disappointing rides.


00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:59.800
Joe thinks Disneyworld is Vegas for kids.


00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:02.700
So, Valerie, what do you do?


00:06:02.700 --> 00:06:05.900
I work in venture capital.
Brewster Jennings, here in Georgetown.


00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:07.200
Oh, cool. Like Net start-ups?


00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:09.200
Exactly. Retail consumer.


00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:11.200
We create pooled investment vehicles.


00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:12.300
It's actually pretty boring.


00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:13.600
You get on a plane.


00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:17.800
Two guys in turbans, seats 1A, 1 B.


00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:21.000
And they look nervous
and they're sweating, they're sweaty


00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:24.100
and they're saying prayers.
What do you do?


00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:25.800
Steve, you have a kid, right?
You're off that plane.


00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:28.000
You're calling the cops.
If we're honest, we all are.


00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:29.600
Joe? You know you are.


00:06:29.600 --> 00:06:32.400
Come on, you see these two guys
on a plane. Turbans.


00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:34.800
Sweating. Prayers. The whole thing.


00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:37.200
What do you say? What's the call?


00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:40.400
Well, Jeff.


00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:42.400
He started it.


00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:45.600
Yeah, every time. Every time we go out.


00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:48.600
He asked me a question.
I gave a full and considered response.


00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:51.200
He was drunk, Joe.
Everybody's had a hard day.


00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:52.900
They're just trying to let off steam.


00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:55.600
By invoking quasi-racist conundra?
He's a parent.


00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:57.800
Is he teaching his four-year-old
to fear all men in turbans?


00:06:57.800 --> 00:07:02.100
It's Diana's birthday.
Jeff's her oldest friend.


00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:05.500
- So?
- So you can't call him a racist pussy.


00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:08.400
It's not funny, Joe.


00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:10.500
It's not funny. It's a very serious subject.


00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:13.400
And if by not keeping quiet while someone
spouts obnoxious crap


00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:16.800
makes you an asshole, then I'm an asshole.
You knew that when you married me.


00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:23.200
How was your trip?


00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:36.900
No! Oh, God.


00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:05.800
- Hey, you cheated.
- No, I didn't! It's a tie.


00:08:06.100 --> 00:08:07.400
Valerie, where's Kim?


00:08:08.700 --> 00:08:11.700
She can't get here
until after lunch. Didn't I tell you?


00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:17.000
Okay. I guess I'll be working at home
this morning.


00:08:16.900 --> 00:08:18.100
Is that okay?


00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:20.200
Yeah. Me and Spongebob got it.


00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:21.700
Break it up. Trevor, don't hit your sister.


00:08:21.700 --> 00:08:24.600
Listen, the Mitchells want to have dinner
on Tuesday.


00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:27.000
But if you want to skip it...


00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:29.400
I promise I'll behave.


00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.300
I promise to behave.


00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:32.900
See, everyone's on their best behavior.


00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:34.700
I love you.


00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:37.700
I'll see you.


00:08:38.600 --> 00:08:40.500
- Bye.
- Bye.


00:08:46.900 --> 00:08:48.700
- Say, "Bye, Mommy."
- Bye.


00:08:48.800 --> 00:08:50.200
- Bye.
- Bye, Mom.


00:08:51.600 --> 00:08:53.300
Do you guys
want to watch some television?


00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:54.800
- Yeah.
- Yeah.


00:08:56.700 --> 00:08:59.000
Counter-proliferation
tracks and thwarts nuclear


00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:03.200
and WMD acquisitions
by rogue nations and non-state actors.


00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:05.400
We're the fastest-growing division
within the Agency.


00:09:05.400 --> 00:09:08.600
Which sounds cool,
but you may have to share a desk.


00:09:08.600 --> 00:09:10.000
Hafiz hired a cleaner.


00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:11.800
Gotta go. Kuala Lumpur just went live.


00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:14.000
- What time did he call this in?
- 1100 hours Zulu time.


00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:17.200
Keep the transaction live.
Trace it all the way to the end user.


00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:19.900
The shipment arrives in Joburg on the 21st.


00:09:19.900 --> 00:09:21.500
It's put in an unmarked container


00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:24.400
and shipped to the Jebel free-trade zone
in Dubai.


00:09:24.300 --> 00:09:27.500
Here. Dr. Jonas and his team at Los Alamos


00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:30.800
have altered the impedance timings of the
spark gaps by a fraction of a nanosecond.


00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:33.000
Val, Chief wants to see you.


00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:34.700
Shut it down.


00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:36.800
Why? We have everything.
We're ready to go.


00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:39.000
We have actual intel on the buyer.


00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:42.400
Sargin Vaziri, Syrian national
based out of Karachi.


00:09:42.300 --> 00:09:45.500
On a wire picked up in Cairo
he talks about nuclear componentry


00:09:45.300 --> 00:09:48.800
from a known source in Pakistan.
He's moving to an unnamed Gulf state.


00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:50.600
Could it be Iraq?


00:09:50.700 --> 00:09:52.600
Vaziri's devoutly Shia.


00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:55.800
Iraq's controlled by Sunnis. Saddam's
Sunni. There's no way this is Iraq.


00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:58.700
Seventh Floor issued a directive
for a joint task force on Iraq.


00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:01.100
I want you to head up operations.


00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:03.300
- Congratulations, Valerie.
- Thank you.


00:10:03.300 --> 00:10:05.600
You can pick your own team.
This is top priority.


00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:08.300
I need 24 hours
to brief my replacement.


00:10:08.700 --> 00:10:10.500
From Monday,
I need your both eyes on Iraq.


00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:11.600
Yes, sir.


00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:15.800
This is coming from across the river.
Down the line, DFU.


00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:23.300
DFU?


00:10:23.900 --> 00:10:25.300
Don't fuck up.


00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:32.500
Congratulations.


00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:34.100
Thanks.


00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:39.200
You can put it there.


00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:03.000
Hey.


00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:04.900
Don't you have a home to go to?


00:11:10.700 --> 00:11:12.400
I thought this went away.


00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:14.200
The DIA released the report Tuesday.


00:11:14.600 --> 00:11:16.500
WINPAC aren't buying
and State kicked it back,


00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:18.600
but it's still making waves
in the Vice President's office.


00:11:19.300 --> 00:11:20.700
You think Joe could do it?


00:11:23.800 --> 00:11:28.300
Well, he's qualified.
He's been there hundreds of times.


00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:30.200
He knows the arena inside out.


00:11:30.200 --> 00:11:33.200
Great. Could you put his credentials
in a memo?


00:11:33.200 --> 00:11:34.800
I want to kick it up the ladder.


00:11:36.200 --> 00:11:37.700
You don't look overjoyed.


00:11:39.900 --> 00:11:42.700
Joe's been working hard
to build his business.


00:11:42.700 --> 00:11:45.400
Then there's the twins.
Money's kind of tight right now.


00:11:46.300 --> 00:11:49.800
He's helped us before.
Could you just ask him to come in?


00:12:07.100 --> 00:12:08.600
Hey, Joe?


00:12:08.600 --> 00:12:12.200
Hey. Nice place you got here. Cozy.


00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:13.400
I need to get you cleared.


00:12:18.100 --> 00:12:19.400
You work in the basement?


00:12:19.700 --> 00:12:22.200
Actually, I work in Georgetown
at Brewster Jennings.


00:12:22.500 --> 00:12:24.500
We're a small firm of venture capitalists.


00:12:24.400 --> 00:12:26.400
Well, that must be interesting work.


00:12:27.500 --> 00:12:28.800
It pays the rent.


00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:41.500
Come in.


00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:43.300
Joe, this is Jack.


00:12:43.400 --> 00:12:44.600
- Hi, Joe Wilson.
- Deputy Chief of CPD.


00:12:44.600 --> 00:12:45.600
It's a pleasure, Ambassador.


00:12:46.300 --> 00:12:47.600
- Hi, Joe Wilson.
- Ambassador.


00:12:48.100 --> 00:12:49.300
- I'll leave you guys to it.
- Joe Wilson.


00:12:49.300 --> 00:12:50.600
- Good morning, Ambassador.
- How are you?


00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:54.100
Joe Wilson. Hello. Joe Wilson. Hi.


00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:58.200
Have a seat.
Can I get you something to drink?


00:12:58.100 --> 00:13:00.400
Coffee would be great. Thank you.


00:13:00.300 --> 00:13:02.100
How do you like it?


00:13:02.100 --> 00:13:03.600
Just black, thanks.


00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:07.300
Ambassador Wilson,
what do you know about yellowcake?


00:13:08.200 --> 00:13:09.600
Yellowcake uranium?


00:13:10.100 --> 00:13:14.400
I believe it's a concentrate
made from uranium ore


00:13:14.300 --> 00:13:16.800
that's used in the fissile material
for weapons programs.


00:13:16.700 --> 00:13:18.100
But I'm not a scientist.


00:13:18.200 --> 00:13:19.500
- Thank you.
- What about Niger?


00:13:21.200 --> 00:13:24.700
I usually pronounce it Niger
to avoid confusion with Nigeria.


00:13:26.600 --> 00:13:30.900
The UN Human Development Index rates it
the least-livable country in the world.


00:13:31.100 --> 00:13:32.900
I started my foreign service there.


00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:35.900
I visited many times
as Ambassador to Gabon.


00:13:35.900 --> 00:13:41.200
And then again as Director of Africa Policy
for President Clinton


00:13:41.200 --> 00:13:42.500
with the NSC.


00:13:43.100 --> 00:13:44.900
I've often met with Prime Minister Mayaki.


00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:47.100
I know the former Foreign Minister,
I know the Minister of Mines.


00:13:47.100 --> 00:13:48.400
I know the country very well.


00:13:48.500 --> 00:13:51.200
The office of the Vice President
has received a report


00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:54.400
concerning a memorandum of sale
between the governments of Niger and Iraq


00:13:54.700 --> 00:13:57.600
for the purchase of 500 tons
of yellowcake uranium ore.


00:13:59.100 --> 00:14:00.800
I don't have to tell you
how serious this allegation is.


00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:01.900
No, sir, you don't.


00:14:02.900 --> 00:14:04.900
This is a request
from the Vice President's office.


00:14:05.900 --> 00:14:07.100
Can you help us?


00:14:08.900 --> 00:14:10.200
What do you have in mind?


00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:45.100
How can Niger help its old friend America?


00:15:45.600 --> 00:15:50.000
In the summer of 2001, Iraq sought
to purchase 60,000 high-alloy


00:15:49.800 --> 00:15:53.800
7075 T6 aluminum tubes
manufactured in China.


00:15:54.200 --> 00:15:57.100
The high spec of these tubes
led us to conclude


00:15:57.100 --> 00:15:59.900
that they were intended
for the enrichment of uranium


00:15:59.900 --> 00:16:03.700
and as such provide proof
that Saddam is building a nuclear bomb.


00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:06.600
In August of 2001, Jay Turner, that's me,


00:16:07.700 --> 00:16:10.500
flew to Vienna to meet
with the IAEA scientists.


00:16:10.500 --> 00:16:13.700
I produced this report,
aspects of which represent


00:16:13.600 --> 00:16:16.700
the CIA's present position.
I'm happy to take questions.


00:16:16.700 --> 00:16:21.400
The INR concluded late last year that
these tubes are probably for artillery use.


00:16:21.300 --> 00:16:24.800
The DOE agreed they exactly matched
those used by Iraq for artillery rockets.


00:16:24.700 --> 00:16:26.000
Where are the tubes?


00:16:26.100 --> 00:16:27.300
WINPAC has them.


00:16:27.900 --> 00:16:29.100
We've examined them.


00:16:29.400 --> 00:16:33.100
And this is my point.
None of you guys have even seen the tubes.


00:16:34.900 --> 00:16:36.300
I've seen them.


00:16:37.600 --> 00:16:39.300
And when was that?


00:16:39.200 --> 00:16:42.400
When I led the covert team
that intercepted them in Jordan,


00:16:42.400 --> 00:16:45.500
brought back samples,
and delivered them to you guys at WINPAC.


00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:49.700
And I take it you're not a nuclear expert.


00:16:50.900 --> 00:16:54.100
These tubes are a match


00:16:54.100 --> 00:16:58.100
for those designed by German scientist
Gernot Zippe in the '50s.


00:16:58.000 --> 00:17:00.400
You're right. I'm no nuclear expert


00:17:00.400 --> 00:17:05.300
but Dr. Houston Wood at
the University of Virginia Atomic Facility is.


00:17:06.200 --> 00:17:11.800
He also knows Dr. Zippe and he told him
that the wall thickness of the Iraqi tubes


00:17:11.600 --> 00:17:14.500
was 3 or 4 times the thickness
of his design.


00:17:14.900 --> 00:17:19.400
Right, and he also said that the length
of the tubes is twice that of Zippe's design.


00:17:19.300 --> 00:17:21.700
In fact, he said that the only thing
that was similar


00:17:21.700 --> 00:17:24.300
between his tubes and the aluminum tubes


00:17:24.300 --> 00:17:26.100
was that they were both made of aluminum.


00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:30.600
A metal that hasn't been used
in gas centrifuges since 1952.


00:17:31.100 --> 00:17:35.700
I went to Vienna. Okay? Canada.
And I've been working on this for months.


00:17:35.600 --> 00:17:37.900
There are centrifuges. Fact.


00:17:37.900 --> 00:17:40.800
So, basically, they're your tubes


00:17:40.800 --> 00:17:43.400
and if we don't let you win,
you're taking them home.


00:17:44.400 --> 00:17:45.500
That's pathetic.


00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:48.100
Joe, no one's saying you're wrong here,


00:17:48.100 --> 00:17:51.800
but if you're right, it's huge,
so, we ask the question.


00:17:52.700 --> 00:17:55.400
Right? We have to ask the question.


00:18:02.900 --> 00:18:05.500
Niger has two uranium mines
in the Sahara desert.


00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:07.100
One is flooded.


00:18:07.100 --> 00:18:09.400
The other is run by COGEMA,
a French subsidiary


00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:11.400
jointly controlled
by the Japanese and Germans.


00:18:11.900 --> 00:18:15.900
Five hundred tons of yellowcake
is not an off-the-books size transaction.


00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:20.900
It represents a 40% production increase
in the nation's annual output of uranium.


00:18:20.700 --> 00:18:23.500
A sale that size
would leave a huge paper trail.


00:18:24.800 --> 00:18:28.700
Any documentation would, by law,
have to be signed by the Prime Minister,


00:18:29.400 --> 00:18:31.400
Foreign Minister, and the Minister of Mines.


00:18:31.800 --> 00:18:33.500
But say it was an off-the-books deal.


00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:36.900
How do you hide the transportation
of 500 tons of anything,


00:18:36.800 --> 00:18:39.100
let alone lightly-refined uranium?


00:18:39.100 --> 00:18:43.400
You're talking 50 semi-tractor trucks
on one road through villages


00:18:43.300 --> 00:18:46.700
where nothing passed for months
except maybe one bush taxi.


00:18:46.500 --> 00:18:48.500
It would be the biggest event for months.


00:18:48.500 --> 00:18:52.100
To say they forgot
is like kids forgetting Christmas.


00:18:52.900 --> 00:18:54.700
You have the droughts of the '70s and '80s


00:18:54.700 --> 00:18:58.600
which brought millions of dollars
in US aid which continues today.


00:18:58.900 --> 00:19:02.700
It doesn't make any sense that the Nigerians
would compromise that lifeline.


00:19:02.500 --> 00:19:06.500
For that reason and for all the reasons
that I've been telling you,


00:19:07.700 --> 00:19:10.500
it is my opinion that this sale
could not have happened.


00:19:14.500 --> 00:19:16.700
So, what happens next?


00:19:17.600 --> 00:19:21.000
Well, they write a report,
give it to the analysts.


00:19:21.000 --> 00:19:25.100
It will be rewritten, then kicked upstairs
and combined with other reports they get.


00:19:25.800 --> 00:19:26.900
What?


00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:30.200
I just think it's ludicrous that they're gonna
send somebody all the way over there


00:19:30.200 --> 00:19:32.500
and spend all that money
for the same conclusion.


00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:36.200
You can't compile intelligence
from a single source.


00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:38.300
That's not intelligence. That's an opinion.


00:19:38.200 --> 00:19:40.000
Trust me. It's a fact.


00:19:41.000 --> 00:19:42.800
- Says who?
- Says me.


00:19:42.700 --> 00:19:45.900
You're just a teeny-weeny tiny cog
in a giant machine.


00:19:46.900 --> 00:19:49.300
You did your job. You should feel good.


00:19:49.300 --> 00:19:52.000
They count on that.
That's why they don't pay you.


00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:56.500
I'm not feeling very 007-ish.


00:19:58.300 --> 00:20:00.700
Maybe I can get the kids
to make a medal for you.


00:20:03.300 --> 00:20:06.100
Us 00s prefer gratuitous sex.


00:20:16.500 --> 00:20:20.100
Maybe I can do something about that.


00:20:24.900 --> 00:20:27.400
Angola's holding another round of bidding


00:20:27.400 --> 00:20:31.000
on their deep-water offshore blocks
at the end of the year.


00:20:31.300 --> 00:20:34.200
Chevron, Elf, and Exxon are interested.


00:21:05.400 --> 00:21:07.200
- She did it!
- No, I didn't!


00:21:07.200 --> 00:21:09.200
Okay. Everybody okay?


00:21:09.200 --> 00:21:11.500
Four arms, four legs. No broken bones.


00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:13.700
Hey, kids.
Mr. Wilson, I'm so sorry I'm late.


00:21:13.700 --> 00:21:16.500
- That's fine. Look, guys, Kim's here.
- When's Mommy coming home?


00:21:20.200 --> 00:21:23.400
It's an honor
to meet you at last, Dr. Harper.


00:21:23.400 --> 00:21:27.800
I was unable to attend
your string gravity seminar at MIT


00:21:27.600 --> 00:21:30.300
but I read a transcript.


00:21:30.700 --> 00:21:33.000
Did you read my latest paper on quarks?


00:21:33.600 --> 00:21:38.100
Dr. Harper, I cite your 1995 essay
more than once.


00:21:40.200 --> 00:21:43.300
Dr. Harper's in Cambridge, Massachusetts.


00:21:43.100 --> 00:21:47.900
She received a call yesterday
requesting she stay home for 48 hours.


00:21:49.100 --> 00:21:50.600
I don't understand.


00:21:53.500 --> 00:21:54.500
Who are you?


00:21:55.500 --> 00:22:00.100
I'm sorry for misleading you
but I'm here to ask you the same question,


00:22:01.500 --> 00:22:07.100
because you're not Professor Badawi.
Your name is Dr. Harif Al Fallari.


00:22:06.900 --> 00:22:08.800
You were born in Basra.


00:22:08.800 --> 00:22:11.300
You were lead engineer
at the Osirak nuclear facility


00:22:11.300 --> 00:22:13.900
until you fled Iraq and arrived here,
in Cairo.


00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:18.500
I need names of your colleagues
in the weapons programs.


00:22:19.300 --> 00:22:22.900
The lives of hundreds of thousands
of your people may depend upon it.


00:22:22.700 --> 00:22:24.500
This is absurd.


00:22:24.600 --> 00:22:27.100
You were never tortured? Broken?


00:22:27.000 --> 00:22:30.100
You didn't finally escape
and arrive here in Cairo with nothing?


00:22:33.000 --> 00:22:37.000
No. My name is Bakkar Abdel Badawi.


00:22:37.900 --> 00:22:41.000
I've never been to Basra. I'm a teacher.


00:22:45.300 --> 00:22:47.600
Dr. Fallari had two daughters.


00:22:49.700 --> 00:22:53.500
They were taken by Uday Hussein's
private guard.


00:22:53.300 --> 00:22:55.300
They were never seen again.


00:23:07.700 --> 00:23:11.100
I need names of your colleagues
in the weapons programs.


00:23:47.400 --> 00:23:48.900
Why is the OVP here?


00:23:50.400 --> 00:23:51.500
What?


00:23:57.400 --> 00:23:59.100
Yeah?


00:23:59.300 --> 00:24:00.800
The Vice President's men are here.


00:24:01.800 --> 00:24:02.900
What?


00:24:05.200 --> 00:24:09.900
My name is Scooter Libby.
I am the Chief of Staff to the Vice President.


00:24:11.800 --> 00:24:12.800
You are?


00:24:13.900 --> 00:24:18.500
Dave. I'm an analyst in Non-Proliferation.


00:24:21.000 --> 00:24:24.100
What can you tell the Vice President
about aluminum tubes?


00:24:24.700 --> 00:24:27.300
I didn't realize that was
what we were gonna be talking about here.


00:24:30.200 --> 00:24:32.400
Relax, will you?
The Veep's just dotting the I's.


00:24:32.400 --> 00:24:33.400
Come on, Jim.


00:24:33.500 --> 00:24:35.700
The only time the Vice President
comes to Langley is to cut a ribbon.


00:24:35.700 --> 00:24:36.800
Cheney doesn't trust us.


00:24:36.900 --> 00:24:39.200
This shit with Dick goes back 30 years.
It will blow over.


00:24:39.800 --> 00:24:41.800
Hey, Val, where are we on Iraq?


00:24:42.700 --> 00:24:45.400
We need to find sources
that we can rely on.


00:24:46.700 --> 00:24:48.200
We need to get in close.


00:24:48.700 --> 00:24:51.800
Jim, Val thinks she can get us
inside the weapons program.


00:24:53.800 --> 00:24:54.800
How?


00:24:57.200 --> 00:24:59.100
In three weeks
you have to come back again, okay?


00:24:59.000 --> 00:25:00.100
Thank you for everything.


00:25:02.800 --> 00:25:04.800
Sorry, there's nothing I can do.


00:25:06.400 --> 00:25:07.400
God bless.


00:25:09.300 --> 00:25:10.300
Come on.


00:25:11.900 --> 00:25:13.000
I said, come on!


00:25:23.100 --> 00:25:26.100
Dr. Hassan,
is there somewhere we could talk?


00:25:27.800 --> 00:25:29.900
How long is it since you saw your brother?


00:25:32.000 --> 00:25:33.200
1992.


00:25:33.900 --> 00:25:37.700
Before that, in '83, he came here
for an engineering conference.


00:25:37.600 --> 00:25:41.700
Twice in 25 years.
We try to stay in contact. It's difficult.


00:25:43.800 --> 00:25:45.300
Would you like to go back and see him?


00:25:48.500 --> 00:25:50.400
You want me to become a spy?


00:25:51.300 --> 00:25:54.300
We need to ask Hammad some questions.


00:25:54.300 --> 00:25:57.800
- Do you think he'd answer...
- I am a doctor. I work hard.


00:25:57.800 --> 00:26:01.300
I'm also a mother.
I have a small daughter and I'm all she has.


00:26:02.300 --> 00:26:06.600
We could help your brother.
Right now he's extremely valuable to us.


00:26:06.500 --> 00:26:10.000
And to Saddam.
The Mukhabarat watch him night and day.


00:26:12.300 --> 00:26:13.600
He could come here.


00:26:14.600 --> 00:26:17.000
He's an expert physicist. He'd have a job.


00:26:17.900 --> 00:26:20.200
His children, his family would be safe.


00:26:20.200 --> 00:26:22.800
You, your daughter could see him
whenever you want.


00:26:24.400 --> 00:26:26.000
Can you help us?


00:26:26.200 --> 00:26:28.600
I will not do anything to help you.
I don't know you.


00:26:28.600 --> 00:26:30.400
If you care about Iraq, about your country...


00:26:30.300 --> 00:26:31.800
My country is America now.


00:26:32.900 --> 00:26:35.700
- Trust me, if there was another way...
- I don't trust you.


00:26:35.800 --> 00:26:37.300
I don't trust you at all.


00:26:41.300 --> 00:26:45.500
We're going to war. And your brother's
gonna be right in the middle of it.


00:26:54.100 --> 00:26:57.100
If the Iraqi regime wishes peace


00:26:57.100 --> 00:27:00.900
it will immediately
and unconditionally forswear,


00:27:00.900 --> 00:27:04.800
disclose and remove or destroy
all weapons of mass destruction.


00:27:05.000 --> 00:27:06.900
- Come in.
- They're back.


00:27:06.800 --> 00:27:09.700
If Iraq's regime defies us again,


00:27:10.400 --> 00:27:14.800
the world must move deliberately
and decisively to hold Iraq to account.


00:27:19.300 --> 00:27:20.600
Don't make jokes.


00:27:35.900 --> 00:27:38.000
He thinks I don't understand
how serious it is?


00:27:39.500 --> 00:27:44.200
Weeks and weeks of 15-hour days.
We've been back over this and over this.


00:27:46.200 --> 00:27:48.000
All right, that's it. I'm going to handle this.


00:27:50.000 --> 00:27:52.800
We've been over this data with you
five, six times now.


00:27:53.200 --> 00:27:55.700
And we don't know
how you want us to play this.


00:27:59.300 --> 00:28:03.400
Let me level with you here, Paul.
I don't know what these tubes are for.


00:28:04.100 --> 00:28:07.300
There could be something to this,
from everything you're saying


00:28:07.300 --> 00:28:08.900
- but very likely not, right?
- Exactly.


00:28:09.100 --> 00:28:10.800
Let me ask a question.


00:28:10.800 --> 00:28:13.800
When you say,
"We don't really know how to play this,"


00:28:13.800 --> 00:28:14.800
what do you mean?


00:28:15.300 --> 00:28:17.200
I mean to say that I don't know
how to say it any other way...


00:28:17.200 --> 00:28:18.700
You didn't say "I," you said "we."


00:28:19.500 --> 00:28:22.300
So, you and the others had discussed
how to play these briefings.


00:28:22.300 --> 00:28:25.200
Why does the CIA
feel the need to play these briefings?


00:28:25.100 --> 00:28:27.900
No, what I mean is,
I didn't mean what I just said.


00:28:27.900 --> 00:28:30.400
Which part? The last part?
Or other things, too?


00:28:30.400 --> 00:28:32.200
I'm sorry. I'm getting a little confused.


00:28:32.100 --> 00:28:33.900
- Do you want me to come back?
- No. God, no.


00:28:34.600 --> 00:28:37.500
- You don't know why I'm here, do you?
- No.


00:28:37.400 --> 00:28:42.500
In 1991, the United States invaded Iraq,
and afterwards weapons inspectors


00:28:42.400 --> 00:28:45.900
discovered Saddam was six months off
enriching uranium


00:28:45.700 --> 00:28:49.600
to sufficiently high specifications
to make a nuclear bomb.


00:28:50.100 --> 00:28:52.300
He had fissile material.


00:28:53.300 --> 00:28:57.700
Not a single person in the CIA
had the slightest clue


00:28:57.600 --> 00:29:00.100
that such a program even existed.


00:29:01.700 --> 00:29:06.700
So, now, one decade on are you telling me


00:29:06.600 --> 00:29:12.200
that you're 100% sure these tubes are not
intended to create nuclear weapons?


00:29:12.000 --> 00:29:14.700
One point about intelligence,
nothing is 100%.


00:29:14.600 --> 00:29:17.200
So, what, are you 99% sure? 98%?


00:29:17.200 --> 00:29:19.000
I'm saying that you can't
put an exact figure on it.


00:29:18.900 --> 00:29:21.100
- I'm saying that...
- But if you had to say?


00:29:21.100 --> 00:29:23.000
You cannot be that precise.


00:29:23.000 --> 00:29:24.600
Could you say you're 97% sure?


00:29:25.000 --> 00:29:27.100
Is there a 3% chance you've got this wrong?


00:29:28.300 --> 00:29:30.100
Or four or five?


00:29:31.300 --> 00:29:33.500
Still pretty good odds.
Do you like those odds, Paul?


00:29:34.000 --> 00:29:37.400
Are you willing to put your name to that?
Ready to make that call?


00:29:37.300 --> 00:29:40.300
- I don't make that call, sir.
- Yes, you do, Paul.


00:29:41.300 --> 00:29:44.000
Each time you interpret a piece of data.


00:29:44.500 --> 00:29:47.800
Each time you choose
a maybe over a perhaps


00:29:47.800 --> 00:29:50.700
you make a call, a decision.


00:29:50.700 --> 00:29:55.200
Right now you're making a lot of little
decisions adding up to a big decision.


00:29:56.100 --> 00:29:59.000
But what if there's only
a 1% chance that you're wrong?


00:29:59.000 --> 00:30:01.300
Can you say for sure
that you'll take that chance


00:30:01.300 --> 00:30:03.400
and state as a fact


00:30:03.400 --> 00:30:07.200
that this equipment is not intended
for a nuclear weapons program?


00:30:07.900 --> 00:30:12.400
Do you know what 1% of the population
of this country is?


00:30:13.300 --> 00:30:17.100
It's 3,240,000 souls.


00:30:17.900 --> 00:30:22.800
Okay, sir. Look, we're not machines.
We look at the evidence. We game it out.


00:30:22.700 --> 00:30:25.700
And believe it or not, not everybody agrees
all the time.


00:30:25.600 --> 00:30:27.600
- It's a process.
- It's a process.


00:30:27.600 --> 00:30:29.500
- Yes.
- And not everyone agrees.


00:30:29.400 --> 00:30:30.500
Exactly.


00:30:32.600 --> 00:30:33.700
Who doesn't agree?


00:30:39.800 --> 00:30:42.500
What the hell is Joe Turner
doing next to the DCI?


00:30:42.500 --> 00:30:45.800
Didn't you hear? On Friday,
the DCI took him to the White House.


00:30:45.700 --> 00:30:48.100
He briefed the President
on aluminum tubes.


00:30:48.000 --> 00:30:49.400
You've got to be kidding me.


00:30:50.400 --> 00:30:51.700
That guy's a tool.


00:30:51.600 --> 00:30:54.400
Ready! Aim! Fire!


00:30:55.100 --> 00:30:57.600
It's a dead end.
So, you got a list of Iraqi scientists.


00:30:57.600 --> 00:30:59.300
How do you suggest we get to them?


00:30:59.300 --> 00:31:02.200
The Mukhabarat watch the scientists
night and day.


00:31:02.100 --> 00:31:03.600
Their houses are bugged,
their friends are followed.


00:31:03.500 --> 00:31:05.500
Send in
a team of NOCs by taxi from the north.


00:31:05.500 --> 00:31:07.500
Say you get through the checkpoints
and roadblocks.


00:31:07.400 --> 00:31:08.900
If you showed up in my bedroom
in the dead of night


00:31:08.900 --> 00:31:12.000
asking me to help out Uncle Sam,
I'm going to react unpredictably.


00:31:11.900 --> 00:31:13.900
Given the theater, it's all too high-risk.


00:31:13.900 --> 00:31:15.900
Even if we get to them,
they won't come out alone.


00:31:15.900 --> 00:31:17.900
They'll want to bring their family,
their children, their kids.


00:31:17.900 --> 00:31:20.300
We'll get down south to Basra,
we'll ask for Jordan's help.


00:31:20.200 --> 00:31:22.300
Give me two months.
I'll give you two or three.


00:31:22.300 --> 00:31:25.200
No, I have 29 names.
I need to get to them all.


00:31:25.200 --> 00:31:28.400
The wall's too high, Val.
What do you want to do, train a mouse?


00:31:28.300 --> 00:31:29.400
Maybe.


00:31:34.200 --> 00:31:37.100
Hey. Did I wake you?


00:31:43.600 --> 00:31:45.600
It's 3:45 in the morning.


00:31:46.400 --> 00:31:48.700
I got to be at the airport in 45 minutes.


00:31:50.100 --> 00:31:53.400
How long this time?
Do we need childcare tomorrow?


00:31:53.400 --> 00:31:55.100
I left it on a Post-it.


00:31:55.800 --> 00:31:57.600
Of course. It's on the Post-it.


00:31:58.700 --> 00:32:01.200
Look, I didn't want to wake you.


00:32:02.400 --> 00:32:05.500
All we've been doing is leaving Post-its
for each other for months.


00:32:06.200 --> 00:32:07.700
The fridge is like a dead letter drop.


00:32:14.500 --> 00:32:15.500
Shit.


00:32:16.200 --> 00:32:20.600
I sound like some old... God.


00:32:28.800 --> 00:32:30.400
I don't know where you go.


00:32:32.800 --> 00:32:35.900
I don't know who you meet.
I don't know if you're in jail somewhere


00:32:35.800 --> 00:32:38.200
or in a ditch somewhere in Jordan, Beirut.


00:32:41.600 --> 00:32:45.900
If you went missing, I couldn't tell anybody
because you were never there.


00:32:51.000 --> 00:32:52.300
I don't know where you go.


00:32:54.200 --> 00:32:55.700
I'm going to Cleveland.


00:32:59.200 --> 00:33:03.100
It's on the Post-it.


00:33:16.300 --> 00:33:17.700
Have a good day.


00:33:54.300 --> 00:33:55.700
You have two of these
in your luggage.


00:33:55.700 --> 00:33:57.100
This is the only pen we want you to use.


00:33:57.900 --> 00:34:00.500
The ink on this pen
is visible for 10 seconds.


00:34:00.500 --> 00:34:02.500
Only when given the correct
chemical fixative can it be read.


00:34:02.500 --> 00:34:05.800
If the Mukhabarat see any of this they will
do things to me that you cannot imagine.


00:34:06.600 --> 00:34:09.300
Tell me what you need to know.
I will memorize it.


00:34:09.300 --> 00:34:12.500
We have 50 very specific questions,
some extremely technical.


00:34:12.500 --> 00:34:15.200
You have 206 bones in your body.


00:34:15.700 --> 00:34:19.300
Do you want their names
in English, Latin or Arabic?


00:34:24.400 --> 00:34:25.500
How do you feel?


00:34:34.200 --> 00:34:37.600
If anyone stops you,
anyone asks you anything,


00:34:39.500 --> 00:34:41.800
stay calm. You're just visiting your brother.


00:34:42.400 --> 00:34:43.500
Keep it simple.


00:34:43.500 --> 00:34:45.100
How do you do it?


00:34:46.000 --> 00:34:47.800
Lie to someone to their face?


00:34:49.000 --> 00:34:50.100
Huh?


00:34:55.000 --> 00:34:58.900
You have to know why you're lying


00:34:59.800 --> 00:35:01.100
and never forget the truth.


00:35:09.000 --> 00:35:10.000
It's time.


00:35:13.700 --> 00:35:15.200
Are you ready?


00:35:38.700 --> 00:35:42.100
Welcome to Queen Alia
International Airport.


00:35:48.000 --> 00:35:51.200
The Mukhabarat is watching the flight desk
on this side.


00:36:16.600 --> 00:36:18.700
Based on what you know right now,


00:36:18.800 --> 00:36:21.700
how close
is Saddam Hussein's government...


00:36:21.600 --> 00:36:25.500
How close is that government
to developing a nuclear capability?


00:36:26.600 --> 00:36:30.300
You'll get different estimates
about precisely how close he is.


00:36:30.300 --> 00:36:33.200
We do know that there have been shipments


00:36:33.100 --> 00:36:36.600
going into Iraq, for instance,
of aluminum tubes


00:36:36.600 --> 00:36:40.400
that really are only suited
for nuclear weapons programs,


00:36:40.300 --> 00:36:41.800
centrifuge programs.


00:36:42.300 --> 00:36:45.400
There will always be some uncertainty


00:36:45.400 --> 00:36:48.500
about how quickly
he can acquire nuclear weapons.


00:36:48.500 --> 00:36:51.200
But we don't want the smoking gun
to be a mushroom cloud.


00:36:52.300 --> 00:36:54.000
It's a coordinated leak.


00:36:54.000 --> 00:36:56.500
Someone in the O VP leaked a story
to The New York Times.


00:36:56.500 --> 00:36:58.400
Now they're all across the networks
quoting the leak.


00:36:58.800 --> 00:37:01.700
"Smoking gun?" "Mushroom Cloud?"
They're using the same words.


00:37:02.000 --> 00:37:03.000
It's a coordinated leak.


00:37:03.000 --> 00:37:04.100
I'm coming home.


00:37:04.200 --> 00:37:05.800
We have been able to intercept
and prevent him


00:37:05.800 --> 00:37:07.900
from acquiring
through this particular channel


00:37:08.900 --> 00:37:12.200
the kinds of tubes
that are necessary to build a centrifuge.


00:37:12.600 --> 00:37:15.000
I always close the door,
I always roll up the window.


00:37:15.000 --> 00:37:16.200
Yeah, but you can smell it.


00:37:16.300 --> 00:37:18.100
What would you have me do, roll up a towel


00:37:18.000 --> 00:37:20.000
and hide in the room
like a teenager smoking?


00:37:20.000 --> 00:37:21.500
Or sandbag my study?


00:37:21.500 --> 00:37:24.500
- Just go out on the deck.
- It's minus 10 degrees outside.


00:37:24.900 --> 00:37:25.900
Steve, help me.


00:37:26.800 --> 00:37:30.300
You're missing the whole point. A cigar,
you want the Winston Churchill vibe,


00:37:30.200 --> 00:37:32.600
the slippers, the crackling fire.


00:37:32.600 --> 00:37:35.300
Or musty books, like a faithful dog.


00:37:35.300 --> 00:37:37.800
You don't want to be outside
in a goose down freezing your balls off


00:37:37.800 --> 00:37:38.800
alone in the dark.


00:37:38.800 --> 00:37:41.800
So, don't think Churchill.
Think Scott of the Antarctic.


00:37:44.300 --> 00:37:45.300
I quit.


00:37:45.200 --> 00:37:47.300
Can I ask a dumb question?
What is an aluminum tube?


00:37:47.300 --> 00:37:51.400
It's a centrifuge. It enriches uranium.


00:37:51.400 --> 00:37:52.400
How?


00:37:52.400 --> 00:37:54.300
Nobody knows.


00:37:54.300 --> 00:37:56.400
They do know what they're for. Come on.


00:37:56.400 --> 00:37:58.500
Have you read about this, Valerie?


00:37:58.600 --> 00:38:00.800
Oh, I was away last week on business.


00:38:00.800 --> 00:38:03.700
Basically, Saddam bought these tubes
and we nailed him.


00:38:03.600 --> 00:38:05.500
We have them
and they're packed with uranium.


00:38:05.500 --> 00:38:06.600
They're packed with uranium?


00:38:06.600 --> 00:38:08.000
They're packed with uranium!


00:38:09.300 --> 00:38:10.700
My expert husband.


00:38:10.700 --> 00:38:13.800
Okay, right. So, they're for purifying,
but the bomb comes later.


00:38:13.800 --> 00:38:16.400
Basically, you boil it up
and you make the big one. Right?


00:38:16.300 --> 00:38:18.800
No, says who? It's a bunch of tubes, Jeff.


00:38:18.700 --> 00:38:20.600
Everything you read!
The New York Times. You're right.


00:38:20.600 --> 00:38:22.800
Joe, you know about this stuff.
What's your hunch on this?


00:38:22.800 --> 00:38:24.900
I don't know anything about tubes.
I'm not qualified.


00:38:24.900 --> 00:38:25.900
I think...


00:38:26.000 --> 00:38:30.400
It's a pretext! 50% of Americans
think Saddam blew up the towers.


00:38:30.300 --> 00:38:32.300
Yeah, but you can't say
he's not a threat!


00:38:32.300 --> 00:38:34.200
- I agree!
- Saddam's not a threat!


00:38:34.200 --> 00:38:35.400
Nobody's saying that.


00:38:35.500 --> 00:38:37.000
If we got rid of Hitler in the '30s...


00:38:37.000 --> 00:38:40.300
He's not Hitler! I'm sorry, he's not Hitler.
He's Saddam.


00:38:40.200 --> 00:38:45.200
We put him there. Why? It suited us!
He's our fault, always was. He's not a threat!


00:38:45.000 --> 00:38:47.100
Have you met him, Fred?
Have you met Saddam?


00:38:47.400 --> 00:38:50.300
Has Saddam looked you in the eye
and threatened you?


00:38:51.800 --> 00:38:53.000
Has he threatened to kill you?


00:38:54.800 --> 00:38:56.300
You don't know what you're talking about.


00:39:00.500 --> 00:39:03.800
- All right.
- I think that's probably true.


00:39:04.400 --> 00:39:06.700
I'm guilty of part of that.


00:39:06.700 --> 00:39:08.400
Dessert? Coffee? Any takers?


00:39:08.400 --> 00:39:10.500
- It was delicious.
- I do think he had a point.


00:39:10.500 --> 00:39:11.800
He's making a separate point.


00:39:11.800 --> 00:39:13.700
Obviously, this needs to go elsewhere.


00:39:15.200 --> 00:39:18.600
We have a rule in our house.
No politics at the table.


00:39:19.000 --> 00:39:20.700
It always ends in a squabble.


00:39:21.100 --> 00:39:23.400
Nobody knows what's going on over there.


00:39:23.400 --> 00:39:25.400
At the end of the day, who really knows?


00:39:26.200 --> 00:39:29.500
That's right, Sue. Who knows?


00:40:06.300 --> 00:40:07.300
Hammad.


00:41:38.300 --> 00:41:39.500
Cuckoo!


00:42:08.300 --> 00:42:10.200
They have given me questions for you.


00:42:12.000 --> 00:42:13.500
What questions?


00:42:13.500 --> 00:42:18.300
How close is your program to a warhead?
When and where is the first test scheduled?


00:42:18.200 --> 00:42:20.700
How much 235-grade uranium do you have?


00:42:20.700 --> 00:42:25.600
Identify other scientists of the program.
Who in the military controls the program?


00:42:25.400 --> 00:42:28.000
Which of the... Which...


00:42:29.200 --> 00:42:30.400
What is it?


00:42:30.400 --> 00:42:32.400
- They don't know?
- What, Hammad?


00:42:32.900 --> 00:42:35.800
The program was completely destroyed
in the '90s.


00:42:35.800 --> 00:42:38.200
The Americans destroyed it.
They know this.


00:42:40.100 --> 00:42:41.200
What else?


00:42:43.400 --> 00:42:46.300
How advanced is the centrifuge facility?


00:42:46.300 --> 00:42:48.900
Which method are you using
to separate fissile isotopes?


00:42:48.800 --> 00:42:50.000
This is insane.


00:42:51.100 --> 00:42:53.300
We don't have the spare parts
to keep a tank on the road.


00:42:54.500 --> 00:42:58.300
I have to work at a plant
which develops fertilizer. They know.


00:43:02.200 --> 00:43:04.000
They know this. They must know.


00:43:08.300 --> 00:43:09.800
You need to see this.


00:43:14.700 --> 00:43:17.100
We need to get Jack to see this, and Bill.


00:43:18.600 --> 00:43:21.200
Ambassador Wilson
was the last American official


00:43:21.200 --> 00:43:23.300
to meet with Saddam Hussein.


00:43:23.300 --> 00:43:26.000
It was 1990, and it was a pretty scary time.


00:43:26.600 --> 00:43:29.300
Saddam threatened
that he was going to execute


00:43:29.200 --> 00:43:32.900
anybody sheltering
people he called foreigners.


00:43:32.900 --> 00:43:34.800
Ambassador Wilson
called a press conference


00:43:34.700 --> 00:43:36.700
and appeared with a noose around his neck.


00:43:37.900 --> 00:43:40.100
And he said, the press reports,


00:43:40.100 --> 00:43:43.900
"If the choice is to allow Americans
to be taken as hostages


00:43:43.700 --> 00:43:47.400
"or to be executed,
I'll bring my own fucking rope."


00:43:48.800 --> 00:43:50.600
Saddam backed down


00:43:50.600 --> 00:43:54.100
and Ambassador Wilson
helped thousands get safely home.


00:43:54.100 --> 00:43:56.200
When he himself came home
to the United States


00:43:56.200 --> 00:43:58.600
he was warmly greeted by our President,


00:43:58.600 --> 00:44:02.400
who took him to the Oval Office
and introduced him to the War Cabinet


00:44:02.300 --> 00:44:04.000
as an American hero.


00:44:05.500 --> 00:44:08.900
That's not quite right. It was
the Roosevelt Room, not the Oval Office.


00:44:12.100 --> 00:44:13.200
In the middle, please?


00:44:13.200 --> 00:44:16.000
Does Saddam pose an imminent threat
to national security?


00:44:16.900 --> 00:44:20.800
Zahraa's brother worked with
500 nuclear scientists at the Safa factory.


00:44:20.900 --> 00:44:23.800
In '91 it was blanket-bombed by B-52's.


00:44:23.800 --> 00:44:26.300
Hussein Kamel kept the scientists together,


00:44:26.300 --> 00:44:27.900
threatening to kill them
if they tried to leave.


00:44:27.900 --> 00:44:30.000
But sanctions destroyed the economy.


00:44:30.000 --> 00:44:34.100
And when Kamel was executed in '95,
the team just drifted apart.


00:44:34.400 --> 00:44:36.900
They're all saying the same thing. Everyone.


00:44:37.100 --> 00:44:38.300
There's no weapons program.


00:44:39.000 --> 00:44:42.400
You've got 30 nuclear scientists
interrogated by Iraqis in Iraq


00:44:42.300 --> 00:44:43.400
all saying the same thing.


00:44:43.400 --> 00:44:46.500
Jim, these people took a great risk.


00:44:46.400 --> 00:44:49.000
To bring us what?
I could have saved us the airfare.


00:44:49.000 --> 00:44:51.000
The White House is getting stove-piped.


00:44:51.900 --> 00:44:56.000
Someone is cherry-picking raw data
and serving it up to the press as fact.


00:44:55.900 --> 00:44:58.800
Then they look to us to confirm it.
It's bullshit.


00:44:58.800 --> 00:45:00.800
One of Saddam's ministers asked him


00:45:00.700 --> 00:45:05.100
why he had executed a certain official
who'd been a loyal supporter.


00:45:06.500 --> 00:45:10.700
Saddam said,
"I would rather kill my friends in error


00:45:12.500 --> 00:45:14.700
"than to allow my enemies to live."


00:45:15.800 --> 00:45:17.600
For me, that's the mark of a monster.


00:45:20.300 --> 00:45:24.500
Vice President Cheney,
members of Congress,


00:45:24.500 --> 00:45:27.200
distinguished citizens and fellow citizens.


00:45:27.600 --> 00:45:29.600
Every year, by law and by custom


00:45:29.600 --> 00:45:32.500
we meet here
to consider the state of the Union.


00:45:32.800 --> 00:45:34.700
- Thank you so much.
- You're welcome.


00:45:36.100 --> 00:45:38.900
Wait, we'd like you to have this coffee mug


00:45:38.800 --> 00:45:40.600
- and some pennants for your kids.
- Thank you.


00:45:40.700 --> 00:45:43.100
Thank you so much for coming
and speaking to us.


00:45:43.100 --> 00:45:44.200
Drive safe out there.


00:45:44.200 --> 00:45:46.400
...the gravest danger in the War on Terror.


00:45:46.400 --> 00:45:48.700
The gravest danger
facing America and the world.


00:45:50.400 --> 00:45:51.800
I'll have a black eye to go, please.


00:45:51.800 --> 00:45:52.900
What's that?


00:45:52.900 --> 00:45:55.000
Two shots of espresso in coffee.
Black coffee.


00:45:58.400 --> 00:46:03.600
US Intelligence indicates Saddam Hussein
has upwards of 30,000 munitions capable


00:46:03.600 --> 00:46:05.400
- of delivering chemical agents.
- Thank you.


00:46:08.100 --> 00:46:11.500
From three Iraqi defectors
we know that Iraq in the late 1990s


00:46:11.400 --> 00:46:14.100
had several mobile
biological weapons labs.


00:46:18.300 --> 00:46:22.300
Saddam Hussein had an advanced
nuclear weapons development program,


00:46:24.100 --> 00:46:26.100
had a design for a nuclear weapon,


00:46:27.100 --> 00:46:31.000
and was working on five different methods
of enriching uranium for a bomb.


00:46:32.400 --> 00:46:34.400
The British government has learned
that Saddam Hussein


00:46:34.500 --> 00:46:38.800
recently sought significant quantities
of uranium from Africa.


00:46:41.500 --> 00:46:44.000
Our intelligence sources tell us
that he has attempted to purchase


00:46:43.900 --> 00:46:48.400
high-strength aluminum tubes
suitable for nuclear weapons production.


00:46:50.000 --> 00:46:54.600
This nation fights reluctantly
because we know the cost.


00:46:54.400 --> 00:46:56.700
We dread the days of mourning
that always come.


00:46:58.000 --> 00:46:59.400
We seek peace.


00:47:00.300 --> 00:47:01.900
We strive for peace.


00:47:02.800 --> 00:47:06.200
And sometimes peace must be defended.


00:47:07.700 --> 00:47:08.800
In Baghdad,


00:47:08.900 --> 00:47:12.800
42 cruise missiles and bunker buster bombs
from F-117's


00:47:12.700 --> 00:47:14.400
were aimed at Iraq's leaders.


00:47:14.300 --> 00:47:15.500
...campaign called Shock and Awe.


00:47:15.600 --> 00:47:18.700
He vowed the US
will accept no outcome but victory.


00:47:28.500 --> 00:47:31.000
For approximately five to eight minutes.


00:49:18.900 --> 00:49:20.100
Bill? Wait up.


00:49:20.100 --> 00:49:22.900
Every team is combing the desert
looking for WMDs.


00:49:22.800 --> 00:49:24.000
Look, all I need is a couple...


00:49:24.100 --> 00:49:26.000
We don't have the resources, Val!


00:49:26.000 --> 00:49:27.700
- To get these families...
- Listen to me!


00:49:27.600 --> 00:49:30.900
Will you listen to me?
Let's say we extract these guys.


00:49:30.900 --> 00:49:32.200
We bring them home and put them on CNN.


00:49:32.200 --> 00:49:35.400
What do you think they're going to tell us
that the White House wants to hear? Huh?


00:49:35.300 --> 00:49:38.000
"Thank you, and by the way,
there was no nuclear program.


00:49:38.000 --> 00:49:40.900
"There is no WMD. P.S. You all knew that."


00:49:42.300 --> 00:49:43.800
Think about it.
Do you want me to go to the DCI


00:49:43.800 --> 00:49:45.000
and ask him to sign off on his own funeral?


00:49:45.000 --> 00:49:46.600
Bill, I gave my word.


00:49:46.500 --> 00:49:48.800
That's not my problem.
I got bigger problems.


00:49:55.400 --> 00:49:58.000
It's like if there was a baby
on the ledge up on 7th.


00:49:58.000 --> 00:50:00.800
No one would get up and save it
in case the White House wanted it there.


00:50:00.800 --> 00:50:05.100
Bill's right. This is just one snafu in 1,000
that we have right now.


00:50:04.900 --> 00:50:07.900
- These scientists are not our...
- These scientists are the WMD.


00:50:07.900 --> 00:50:11.300
If we can't protect them, they'll run straight
to the first country who can


00:50:11.200 --> 00:50:12.400
and they'll put them to work.


00:50:20.700 --> 00:50:24.200
I never said this.
If anyone ever asks I'll deny all knowledge.


00:50:27.000 --> 00:50:28.600
How quietly can you do this?


00:51:50.900 --> 00:51:53.000
I need to know my family will be safe.


00:51:53.000 --> 00:51:54.700
My wife, my children, we're all in danger.


00:51:55.500 --> 00:51:56.900
Hammad, I know that.


00:51:57.000 --> 00:52:00.700
We'll take care of your family
but we have to move fast, okay?


00:52:00.600 --> 00:52:02.100
How do I know I can trust you?


00:52:02.200 --> 00:52:07.500
Hammad, listen to me, do exactly as I say.
We won't let you down.


00:52:11.100 --> 00:52:12.400
The US Military has reported


00:52:12.300 --> 00:52:15.900
the death of another five US soldiers
on Wednesday.


00:52:15.900 --> 00:52:19.900
One soldier died after being struck
by a bomb while on foot patrol.


00:52:19.800 --> 00:52:21.900
Reported killed across the country.


00:52:21.900 --> 00:52:25.200
Official Iraqi figures show that 966...


00:52:25.900 --> 00:52:29.000
The British government has learned
that Saddam Hussein...


00:52:29.000 --> 00:52:30.700
...significant quantities of uranium


00:52:31.200 --> 00:52:32.300
from Africa.


00:52:34.600 --> 00:52:36.500
The British government has learned
that Saddam Hussein


00:52:36.400 --> 00:52:40.800
recently sought significant quantities
of uranium from Africa.


00:52:41.500 --> 00:52:44.100
Listen, Pete, I want to ask you
something. It's very important.


00:52:45.100 --> 00:52:49.800
Is it possible that the President is referring
to another African country, not Niger?


00:52:50.800 --> 00:52:52.600
I've seen the INR. It's Niger.


00:52:53.300 --> 00:52:55.500
He's referring specifically
to yellowcake from Niger. Why?


00:52:59.400 --> 00:53:03.500
I'm the source. I went to Niger. It's wrong.
It's not true.


00:53:04.300 --> 00:53:05.500
I see.


00:53:07.600 --> 00:53:09.400
What exactly are you proposing to do?


00:53:11.400 --> 00:53:12.800
I don't know what I'm gonna do.


00:53:13.400 --> 00:53:14.500
Do you want my advice?


00:53:14.600 --> 00:53:16.900
Do nothing. You already did your job.


00:53:16.900 --> 00:53:19.600
You did your best, you came home.
End of story.


00:53:20.400 --> 00:53:23.600
We're talking about Niger.
Yellowcake from Niger.


00:53:23.500 --> 00:53:26.800
I don't have to go all the way to Africa
to know something's messed up here.


00:53:27.200 --> 00:53:28.400
Three months and what have we found?


00:53:28.900 --> 00:53:32.700
No centrifuges, no yellowcake,
no bio, no WMDs.


00:53:32.900 --> 00:53:34.800
You think something's up, here?
Join the line.


00:53:34.900 --> 00:53:36.900
It stretches all the way from State
to the Pentagon and back.


00:53:36.800 --> 00:53:38.700
Why hasn't anybody stepped forward?


00:53:38.600 --> 00:53:39.900
Why do you think, Joe?


00:53:41.000 --> 00:53:42.500
We went to war.


00:53:42.800 --> 00:53:45.200
Listen, as your friend now,


00:53:46.300 --> 00:53:49.500
just be smart.


00:53:49.400 --> 00:53:51.300
You have a wife and a family.


00:53:51.700 --> 00:53:54.600
We're talking
about the President of the United States.


00:53:54.500 --> 00:53:56.000
The White House.


00:53:56.000 --> 00:53:58.700
Go take a long look in the mirror
and say that again.


00:54:14.600 --> 00:54:15.800
What's wrong?


00:54:16.400 --> 00:54:17.700
Nothing.


00:54:19.300 --> 00:54:20.300
I'm just tired.


00:54:21.100 --> 00:54:22.700
Are the kids asleep?


00:54:22.700 --> 00:54:24.000
Yeah, they're asleep.


00:54:24.400 --> 00:54:25.500
Okay, good.


00:54:27.900 --> 00:54:29.100
I'm gonna go up.


00:54:35.900 --> 00:54:40.200
There are some who feel like
the conditions are such


00:54:40.200 --> 00:54:41.900
that they can attack us there.


00:54:41.900 --> 00:54:43.200
My answer is, bring them on.


00:54:43.800 --> 00:54:47.600
We've got the force necessary
to deal with the security situation.


00:55:31.700 --> 00:55:35.700
There's zero, nada, nothing new here.


00:55:35.700 --> 00:55:38.000
I think the President's statement
at the State of the Union


00:55:37.900 --> 00:55:39.600
goes much broader than the Niger question.


00:55:39.600 --> 00:55:42.900
Is the President's statement correct?


00:55:42.800 --> 00:55:45.800
Yes.
I see nothing that goes broader


00:55:45.600 --> 00:55:49.700
that would indicate there was no basis
for the President's broader statement.


00:55:49.700 --> 00:55:53.600
But, specifically on the yellowcake
from Niger,


00:55:53.500 --> 00:55:56.100
we have acknowledged that that did in fact


00:55:56.100 --> 00:55:57.500
turn out to be a forgery.


00:55:58.000 --> 00:55:59.000
Oh, shit.


00:55:59.100 --> 00:56:00.100
I'm sorry?


00:56:00.100 --> 00:56:01.100
The British report.


00:56:03.000 --> 00:56:04.100
Um...


00:56:04.300 --> 00:56:05.700
Mark, clear my morning.


00:56:06.900 --> 00:56:07.900
It was wrong, then?


00:56:08.000 --> 00:56:12.700
Let me do this, David.
On David's specific question.


00:56:12.500 --> 00:56:14.700
I'm going to come back to you on that.


00:56:15.800 --> 00:56:16.900
Fleischer plowed the briefing.


00:56:16.900 --> 00:56:17.900
I saw.


00:56:17.900 --> 00:56:21.200
CBS knows yellowcake was pulled
from Cincinnati 10 weeks ago.


00:56:21.200 --> 00:56:22.500
At the CIA's request.


00:56:22.400 --> 00:56:24.400
They also had
that Gerson wrote both speeches.


00:56:24.400 --> 00:56:26.000
Karl is looking for you. He's unhappy.


00:56:26.000 --> 00:56:28.400
I want a transcript of everything across


00:56:28.400 --> 00:56:33.200
network, blogs, and print citing
Ambassador Wilson, Niger or yellowcake.


00:56:33.100 --> 00:56:36.000
Tell Karl I'll be in my office
straight after I'm done.


00:56:41.100 --> 00:56:43.100
The 5th US Circuit Court of Appeals...


00:56:43.200 --> 00:56:45.000
This has become a trust issue
for the President.


00:56:45.000 --> 00:56:46.300
We can't get behind on this.


00:56:46.900 --> 00:56:48.500
A Democratic-led Senate
Judiciary committee...


00:56:48.500 --> 00:56:50.100
We need to change the story.


00:56:51.600 --> 00:56:52.900
Who is Joe Wilson?


00:56:53.800 --> 00:56:57.000
A new controversy over re-targeting
some of America's nuclear weapons.


00:56:56.900 --> 00:56:58.600
There will be more
at the President's press conference.


00:57:01.600 --> 00:57:02.700
David?


00:57:02.700 --> 00:57:05.900
If someone works at the CIA
and they sent their spouse on a trip,


00:57:07.000 --> 00:57:08.800
would there be a paper trail?


00:57:09.600 --> 00:57:12.800
Any such request would require approval
from the chain of command.


00:57:14.300 --> 00:57:17.300
From the requestor
right up to the Director of Operations.


00:57:17.300 --> 00:57:19.700
Yes, paperwork
would normally be generated.


00:57:20.800 --> 00:57:22.000
Okay.


00:57:24.300 --> 00:57:27.300
Does the President
have the power to declassify information?


00:57:45.900 --> 00:57:47.100
Valerie?


00:57:47.700 --> 00:57:48.800
What?


00:57:52.500 --> 00:57:56.400
"'The CIA's decision to send
retired diplomat Joseph C. Wilson..."


00:57:56.300 --> 00:57:57.400
Further down.


00:58:03.700 --> 00:58:06.300
"Wilson never worked for the CIA
but his wife..."


00:58:06.300 --> 00:58:09.300
"Is an agency operative
on weapons of mass destruction."


00:58:09.200 --> 00:58:10.500
He just went ahead and did it.


00:58:11.600 --> 00:58:13.100
Does this run overseas?


00:58:13.100 --> 00:58:14.900
It's in the newspaper, Valerie.
It's on the news.


00:58:14.900 --> 00:58:17.800
Novak's column. Is he syndicated overseas?


00:58:17.700 --> 00:58:19.000
It's everywhere.


00:58:21.500 --> 00:58:22.500
God.


00:58:43.200 --> 00:58:44.900
Jessica McDowell.
Maureen McDermont.


00:58:44.900 --> 00:58:46.900
- I just flew in from Scotland.
- Valerie, what do you do?


00:58:46.900 --> 00:58:49.600
I work in venture capital.


00:58:49.600 --> 00:58:51.400
Grace Semel. Sigma Chemicals.


00:58:51.400 --> 00:58:53.900
Paris, Milan, Vienna.


00:58:54.100 --> 00:58:55.600
Who are you?


00:58:55.600 --> 00:58:57.900
We need a matrix of everyone
you've come into contact with


00:58:57.900 --> 00:59:00.900
- in a covert capacity.
- I've already started a list.


00:59:00.800 --> 00:59:04.400
Good. We need to get an idea, fast,
of how much this thing bleeds.


00:59:04.400 --> 00:59:08.500
Sir, I have several live-ops at crucial stages.
People in the field


00:59:08.400 --> 00:59:10.600
- in critical windows of operation.
- One thing at a time.


00:59:10.900 --> 00:59:13.800
Make a list, then come back here.
Don't do anything else.


00:59:17.500 --> 00:59:19.300
Why is Internal Security here?


00:59:20.000 --> 00:59:23.900
To help you and us
conduct this damage assessment.


00:59:30.800 --> 00:59:33.400
Ms. Plame? We're going this way.


01:00:06.300 --> 01:00:07.400
The restroom.


01:00:14.000 --> 01:00:15.100
Ms. Plame?


01:00:16.400 --> 01:00:17.500
Ms. Plame?


01:00:23.000 --> 01:00:24.200
Ms. Plame?


01:00:41.000 --> 01:00:42.800
Val? Val!


01:00:43.100 --> 01:00:45.500
Jack, I've got to get a message to Baghdad.


01:00:45.400 --> 01:00:48.700
I've got 15 scientists being taken
to the border today.


01:00:48.700 --> 01:00:50.400
I have to get word to them.


01:00:50.400 --> 01:00:51.700
I don't know what you're talking about.


01:00:51.800 --> 01:00:54.400
Jack, they're packed and ready to go.


01:00:54.800 --> 01:00:56.500
You know what this means.


01:00:59.400 --> 01:01:01.400
- Sorry. I've got to go.
- Ms. Plame.


01:01:02.500 --> 01:01:04.800
Val, can I see you for a minute?


01:01:10.400 --> 01:01:12.000
Take a walk.


01:01:13.600 --> 01:01:16.400
As of this morning,
all CPD operations involving you


01:01:16.400 --> 01:01:17.600
have been suspended.


01:01:18.200 --> 01:01:20.000
Effective immediately,
you're to have no further contact


01:01:20.000 --> 01:01:21.700
with assets or agents in the field.


01:01:21.900 --> 01:01:25.600
Any further involvement in operations
is no longer possible.


01:01:26.300 --> 01:01:28.900
Bill, I have eight, nine teams in the field.


01:01:28.900 --> 01:01:32.500
We have assets
in Kuala Lumpur, Mumbai, Dubai.


01:01:43.000 --> 01:01:45.200
I need to brief my replacement
in the Joint Task Force.


01:01:45.400 --> 01:01:47.500
The head of the JTFI's identity is classified


01:01:47.500 --> 01:01:51.800
- for reasons of operational security.
- I have a critical operation


01:01:51.600 --> 01:01:55.100
- in Baghdad in a major...
- Val, I'm sorry.


01:01:57.100 --> 01:01:58.400
It's over.


01:02:00.500 --> 01:02:02.700
You were a good officer,


01:02:04.900 --> 01:02:06.300
but it's over.


01:02:27.400 --> 01:02:29.800
"Two senior administration officials told me


01:02:29.800 --> 01:02:32.300
"that Wilson's wife
suggested sending him to Niger


01:02:32.300 --> 01:02:34.400
"to investigate the Italian report."


01:02:34.400 --> 01:02:38.200
This comes from the Vice President,
the Chief of Staff, or a top advisor.


01:02:38.100 --> 01:02:39.200
I got to go.


01:02:39.200 --> 01:02:40.400
- Look at my picture.
- I will.


01:02:40.800 --> 01:02:43.300
Trevor won't let me
borrow his Power Ranger.


01:02:43.900 --> 01:02:46.700
- Mommy!
- Did you say please?


01:02:46.700 --> 01:02:49.000
- I said please!
- There's a 1982 act


01:02:48.900 --> 01:02:51.300
that says it's a crime
for a government official


01:02:51.300 --> 01:02:53.900
to knowingly disclose a covert agent.


01:02:53.900 --> 01:02:56.700
It comes with a $50,000 fine
andlor up to 10 years in jail.


01:02:57.700 --> 01:02:59.300
- Don't answer the phone, honey.
- It's been ringing all day.


01:02:59.400 --> 01:03:01.200
Do not... Who have you spoken... Joe?


01:03:01.200 --> 01:03:03.600
- Please don't. Joe, Joe...
- She is. Hello?


01:03:03.600 --> 01:03:06.500
- I'm sorry, honey. Are you okay?
- She's right here.


01:03:08.000 --> 01:03:09.500
It's Lisa.


01:03:12.600 --> 01:03:15.400
- Hello?
- Valerie, your name is in the paper.


01:03:15.700 --> 01:03:17.600
It says you're a CIA agent.


01:03:17.600 --> 01:03:19.600
Look, I can't talk right now.


01:03:20.200 --> 01:03:22.100
- Well, I can't make a comment.
- Mom!


01:03:22.400 --> 01:03:25.500
Look, I'm going
to call you back tomorrow, okay?


01:03:25.400 --> 01:03:26.900
I'm really sorry.


01:03:27.000 --> 01:03:29.000
- Oh, my God.
- Shit.


01:03:30.000 --> 01:03:31.300
It's got to be true.


01:03:37.500 --> 01:03:40.900
Your mom called.
Your uncle. Janey in Chicago.


01:03:40.900 --> 01:03:43.100
I wrote it down there for you.


01:03:43.500 --> 01:03:45.600
And Andrea Mitchell called.


01:03:46.700 --> 01:03:48.500
She said White House sources say


01:03:48.600 --> 01:03:53.700
the real story is not the 16 words,
but Joe Wilson and his wife.


01:03:54.100 --> 01:03:56.300
Did I care to comment?


01:03:56.200 --> 01:03:59.200
Well, I damn well do care to comment,


01:03:59.200 --> 01:04:02.300
and she's asked me on the show
the day after tomorrow.


01:04:02.500 --> 01:04:03.700
No.


01:04:04.500 --> 01:04:07.000
You're not going on TV, Joe.


01:04:13.400 --> 01:04:14.500
Thank you.


01:04:17.200 --> 01:04:20.500
This was clearly designed
as a shot across the bow


01:04:20.500 --> 01:04:22.400
for those who might step forward,


01:04:22.400 --> 01:04:26.100
those unnamed analysts who said
that pressure was put on them


01:04:26.000 --> 01:04:27.400
by the White House, for example,


01:04:28.000 --> 01:04:31.000
would think twice about having
their own family's name


01:04:30.800 --> 01:04:33.800
dragged through this particular mud.


01:04:42.600 --> 01:04:48.000
I didn't prepare for this moment.
I had no plan for this day.


01:04:47.800 --> 01:04:49.500
When did you join?


01:04:50.200 --> 01:04:52.300
'85, straight out of college.


01:04:53.300 --> 01:04:55.600
- Wow, that's...
- Eighteen years.


01:04:55.600 --> 01:04:57.300
So, did they find you, or...


01:04:57.300 --> 01:04:59.100
No, I approached them.


01:04:59.800 --> 01:05:02.100
And did Joe know?


01:05:02.400 --> 01:05:03.600
Yes.


01:05:04.200 --> 01:05:05.500
Your parents?


01:05:05.900 --> 01:05:07.600
Yes, but that's all.


01:05:10.100 --> 01:05:13.000
So, do you have lovers all over the world?


01:05:13.300 --> 01:05:14.700
Do you have a gun?


01:05:14.900 --> 01:05:16.800
Have you killed people?


01:05:18.100 --> 01:05:19.500
I can't. I...


01:05:21.300 --> 01:05:23.300
I can't tell you anything.


01:05:26.100 --> 01:05:28.200
You can't tell me anything.


01:05:28.700 --> 01:05:30.100
Okay. All right.


01:05:30.700 --> 01:05:33.900
So, do you want to go shopping?


01:05:33.800 --> 01:05:36.100
- See a movie? Mani-pedi?
- Diana.


01:05:50.100 --> 01:05:51.300
Hi, Mom.


01:05:54.900 --> 01:05:56.400
Did your wife send you to Niger?


01:05:56.400 --> 01:05:59.200
I was not sent by my wife,
but the issue is not who sent me,


01:05:59.200 --> 01:06:01.000
it's whether or not a crime was committed.


01:06:03.200 --> 01:06:06.100
- I'm going to get it!
- I'm going to get it! I got it!


01:06:06.200 --> 01:06:07.400
Hello?


01:06:09.400 --> 01:06:10.500
Hello?


01:06:10.500 --> 01:06:14.300
Your husband is a communist.
I hope you die, you commie whore.


01:06:14.500 --> 01:06:16.500
- We know where you live.
- Who is this?


01:06:16.500 --> 01:06:18.200
- Trevor!
- Who...


01:06:20.200 --> 01:06:21.300
Beat it!


01:06:24.300 --> 01:06:26.700
Mommy, Trevor won't let me go
on his tractor.


01:06:26.600 --> 01:06:29.800
Okay. So, find something else to play.
I don't...


01:06:31.300 --> 01:06:32.400
Mommy?


01:06:33.900 --> 01:06:35.100
Mommy?


01:06:35.100 --> 01:06:36.700
What? What?


01:06:45.600 --> 01:06:48.600
"He stayed inside for more than two weeks.


01:06:49.800 --> 01:06:51.100
"Then he nibbled..."


01:07:07.300 --> 01:07:08.500
Zahraa?


01:07:09.100 --> 01:07:12.800
Hammad has disappeared.
His wife, his children are missing.


01:07:13.400 --> 01:07:16.500
My uncle in Mansour,
he said they were targeting them.


01:07:16.500 --> 01:07:18.100
They were killing them.


01:07:18.100 --> 01:07:20.000
- Who?
- Hammad's colleagues.


01:07:20.000 --> 01:07:24.400
Dr. Habbuk was shot dead in the street.
Dr. Falli was murdered in his hallway.


01:07:24.900 --> 01:07:27.900
- Listen...
- I know you can't tell me where he is.


01:07:27.800 --> 01:07:30.300
Just tell me you have him.
Please, I beg you.


01:07:30.300 --> 01:07:32.700
I don't need to know anything.
Just tell me he's safe.


01:07:36.900 --> 01:07:38.500
We don't have him.


01:07:41.600 --> 01:07:43.700
You said he would be safe.


01:07:45.100 --> 01:07:47.400
You said we would help you.
You promised.


01:07:48.200 --> 01:07:49.600
I trusted you.


01:07:54.600 --> 01:07:56.500
The Justice Department need to establish


01:07:56.500 --> 01:08:00.000
whether those in the highest office
sought to destroy the career


01:07:59.800 --> 01:08:03.200
of a public servant to punish me
for telling the truth.


01:08:04.600 --> 01:08:07.000
- What's going on?
- What are you doing here?


01:08:16.300 --> 01:08:19.700
Falli. Hubbuk. Who else?


01:08:20.300 --> 01:08:21.400
I don't know what you're talking about.


01:08:21.500 --> 01:08:23.800
Don't bullshit me. Who else is dead?


01:08:24.700 --> 01:08:27.700
You were right.
It was all about the scientists.


01:08:27.600 --> 01:08:29.300
We made a call.


01:08:29.400 --> 01:08:30.500
A call?


01:08:30.500 --> 01:08:34.000
We passed your case files to liaison.
Mossad were already on the same page.


01:08:33.900 --> 01:08:35.600
They've been hunting these guys down
since the invasion.


01:08:35.600 --> 01:08:38.700
You'll drive them underground.
They'll run straight to Iran. Pakistan.


01:08:38.700 --> 01:08:39.900
Valerie, it's not your problem.


01:08:39.900 --> 01:08:42.700
- How can you sleep at night?
- I sleep just fine.


01:08:43.900 --> 01:08:47.000
Now, Carol's mother is here. I'm sorry,
but I'm going to have to ask you to leave.


01:08:47.000 --> 01:08:50.000
It's called counter-proliferation, Jack.


01:08:50.700 --> 01:08:51.900
Counter.


01:08:54.800 --> 01:08:57.400
Linda, are you still here? It's late.


01:09:32.800 --> 01:09:35.600
At the end of the day,
it's of keen interest to me


01:09:35.600 --> 01:09:40.100
whether or not we see Karl Rove
frog-marched out of the White House


01:09:40.000 --> 01:09:43.100
in handcuffs.
And believe me, when I use that name,


01:09:43.100 --> 01:09:44.500
I measure my words.


01:09:52.200 --> 01:09:54.100
- Mr. Wilson!
- Excuse me.


01:09:54.100 --> 01:09:55.800
We came all the way from Portland
for this.


01:09:55.800 --> 01:09:57.000
Hello. Okay.


01:09:57.700 --> 01:10:00.800
My wife and I have never sought publicity,


01:10:01.600 --> 01:10:03.900
but I know when I tell her about
all of the support out here today,


01:10:03.800 --> 01:10:05.700
she'll be thrilled and humbled.


01:10:10.400 --> 01:10:12.600
- Hello?
- Valerie, turn on MSNBC.


01:10:12.600 --> 01:10:14.100
Mom, why can't I have
some juice?


01:10:14.100 --> 01:10:15.300
Okay. Hold on one second.


01:10:15.300 --> 01:10:16.800
They've launched an investigation.


01:10:17.800 --> 01:10:19.400
Ashcroft just announced it.


01:10:19.300 --> 01:10:21.000
They say he's going to convene
a grand jury.


01:10:21.000 --> 01:10:22.600
Hold on a second.


01:10:22.700 --> 01:10:26.300
The FBI now is conducting
a criminal investigation


01:10:26.200 --> 01:10:29.500
into who leaked the name
of the CIA undercover operative...


01:10:29.600 --> 01:10:31.700
I'm going to be back later.
I've got to go over to Fox.


01:10:31.700 --> 01:10:33.600
They want me to comment
on the investigation.


01:10:33.600 --> 01:10:36.500
- Joe, just hold on.
- Valerie, we've got to fight this.


01:10:36.600 --> 01:10:38.100
We cannot... We've got to push back.


01:10:38.200 --> 01:10:40.200
Mom! Where's my doll?


01:10:41.600 --> 01:10:42.600
I've got another call. I gotta go.


01:10:42.600 --> 01:10:44.000
Joe! You have to...


01:10:46.200 --> 01:10:47.300
Joe Wilson.


01:10:47.300 --> 01:10:51.000
Joe, it's Chris Matthews.
I just spoke to Karl Rove.


01:10:50.900 --> 01:10:54.300
He told me, "Wilson's wife is fair game."


01:11:04.100 --> 01:11:06.200
Thank you for coming here.


01:11:06.600 --> 01:11:09.700
I wanted to convey my outrage to you
in person.


01:11:10.400 --> 01:11:12.100
I know it's not easy, but I want you to know


01:11:12.200 --> 01:11:15.700
how much the Agency appreciates
your silence in the light of this matter.


01:11:16.500 --> 01:11:20.300
We can't afford
to have this knife fight go on any longer.


01:11:22.100 --> 01:11:23.800
I get death threats every day.


01:11:23.900 --> 01:11:26.400
People threaten to kill my husband,
hurt my children.


01:11:27.000 --> 01:11:28.000
I went to the Agency


01:11:28.100 --> 01:11:30.500
and I requested security
to protect my family.


01:11:31.100 --> 01:11:35.600
I was declined because, "My circumstances
fall outside budget protocols."


01:11:36.800 --> 01:11:40.800
If this is a knife fight, sir,
right now we're fighting it alone.


01:11:43.400 --> 01:11:45.800
Joe Wilson versus the White House, huh?


01:11:45.700 --> 01:11:48.200
Well, all I can say is good luck.


01:11:48.100 --> 01:11:50.700
But I feel, as a friend, I should tell you


01:11:50.700 --> 01:11:54.300
that those men, those few men
in that building over there,


01:11:54.400 --> 01:11:57.800
are the most powerful men
in the history of the world.


01:11:57.800 --> 01:12:02.300
How much of a stretch do you think it'd be
for them to take on Joe Wilson?


01:12:03.700 --> 01:12:06.700
Joe is out there on his own, Valerie,


01:12:06.600 --> 01:12:08.400
but I know we can trust you.


01:12:09.300 --> 01:12:11.100
Speak to your husband.


01:12:16.700 --> 01:12:20.700
Tucker Carlson says,
"Wilson's wife sent him on a boondoggle."


01:12:20.600 --> 01:12:22.500
Says, "He needed the work."


01:12:22.700 --> 01:12:24.100
Who needs to work for free?


01:12:24.400 --> 01:12:28.400
It's not like Niger is renowned
for its fine dining and celebrated operas.


01:12:29.000 --> 01:12:30.900
It reminds me of Paris.


01:12:33.500 --> 01:12:37.400
Listen. Someone from Vanity Fair called,
they want to do a piece.


01:12:37.300 --> 01:12:40.700
They want to do a full-scale interview,
photographs.


01:12:40.700 --> 01:12:42.500
Tell the whole story.


01:12:42.500 --> 01:12:44.700
What do you think about that?


01:12:45.400 --> 01:12:47.000
What do I think?


01:12:48.900 --> 01:12:52.400
Do I want my photograph in Vanity Fair?
Is that the question?


01:12:52.800 --> 01:12:54.400
Valerie, this is our chance.


01:12:54.700 --> 01:12:57.700
- To do what?
- To tell our side of the story.


01:12:57.900 --> 01:13:01.500
It'll mean a dozen,
maybe 50 TV appearances.


01:13:01.500 --> 01:13:02.800
We have to do that.


01:13:02.800 --> 01:13:05.400
They're killing us on Fox, in the blogs.


01:13:05.400 --> 01:13:07.900
They're drowning us out.
We've got to strike back.


01:13:10.900 --> 01:13:13.000
What? What's wrong? What did I say?


01:13:13.100 --> 01:13:16.800
Don't you get it, Joe?
I mean, where does all of this stop?


01:13:18.600 --> 01:13:20.300
Our address is on the Internet.


01:13:20.200 --> 01:13:22.200
A photo of our house.


01:13:22.300 --> 01:13:24.800
I've changed our phone number, what,
five times now?


01:13:24.800 --> 01:13:28.900
My name... My name is everywhere!
My real name, Joe!


01:13:28.800 --> 01:13:32.300
Where does all of this tough-talk
and publicity and noise,


01:13:32.200 --> 01:13:34.800
and all of this bullshit that you're doing,
where does it get us?


01:13:34.900 --> 01:13:38.400
- Where?
- Andy Card told the Financial Times


01:13:38.500 --> 01:13:43.200
that they are rolling earthmovers
over Joe Wilson."Earthmovers."


01:13:43.200 --> 01:13:46.400
Well, I'm sorry,
you're not going to get me without a fight.


01:13:46.300 --> 01:13:48.500
Not without one hell of a fight.


01:13:48.400 --> 01:13:51.200
It's the White House, Joe.
It's the White House.


01:13:51.200 --> 01:13:53.800
Do you seriously think you can pick a fight
with the White House and win?


01:13:53.800 --> 01:13:56.100
- They'll bury us!
- They'll bury us if we don't!


01:13:56.000 --> 01:13:57.800
- Joe.
- Listen to me, Valerie.


01:13:57.800 --> 01:14:01.200
- No, no, you listen to me!
- Valerie! Valerie! Valerie!


01:14:01.500 --> 01:14:04.100
Does that make me right
if I shout louder than you?


01:14:04.400 --> 01:14:06.600
If I shout louder than you, am I right?


01:14:06.600 --> 01:14:10.800
If I'm the White House
and I shout a million times louder than you,


01:14:10.700 --> 01:14:12.300
does that make me right?


01:14:12.300 --> 01:14:14.300
They lied, Valerie.


01:14:14.300 --> 01:14:16.400
They lied. That's the truth.


01:14:17.400 --> 01:14:19.100
Truth. Right.


01:14:20.100 --> 01:14:22.500
Well, by the time they're finished with us,


01:14:22.500 --> 01:14:24.500
- we won't know what that is.
- Mom!


01:14:27.000 --> 01:14:28.200
Great.


01:14:43.000 --> 01:14:44.400
Look, Mommy.


01:14:48.500 --> 01:14:50.100
Is Scooter home?


01:14:57.500 --> 01:15:00.600
- What's that?
- The Senate just finished its investigation.


01:15:00.400 --> 01:15:03.900
The findings of the Select Committee
on Intelligence, all 511 pages.


01:15:04.700 --> 01:15:06.300
Check out page 39.


01:15:12.700 --> 01:15:14.600
- Hi, Daddy!
- Who's the prettiest?


01:15:14.600 --> 01:15:17.000
Hey there, monster. How are you?


01:15:17.900 --> 01:15:21.400
Go get there.
Get some play in before it starts to rain.


01:15:22.700 --> 01:15:23.800
What's that?


01:15:23.700 --> 01:15:26.900
That's the Senate Select Committee
Intelligence report.


01:15:28.000 --> 01:15:29.700
On page 39,


01:15:29.700 --> 01:15:33.500
it says, "The former ambassador's wife
offered up his name."


01:15:33.800 --> 01:15:36.600
It then includes a memorandum
written by Valerie Plame


01:15:36.500 --> 01:15:40.400
which says, "My husband has
good relations with both the Prime Minister


01:15:40.500 --> 01:15:42.000
"and the former Minister of Mines,


01:15:42.000 --> 01:15:44.500
"both of whom could shed light
on this sort of activity."


01:15:44.500 --> 01:15:46.800
- This is exactly what I've been denying.
- No. No.


01:15:46.800 --> 01:15:49.700
I've been to every newspaper,
every television, radio,


01:15:49.600 --> 01:15:51.200
anybody that would listen to me,


01:15:51.200 --> 01:15:53.700
saying my wife did not send me on a junket.


01:15:53.700 --> 01:15:56.300
- I didn't send you. I didn't have that power.
- You sent an e-mail.


01:15:56.200 --> 01:15:57.700
The SSCI found the e-mail.


01:15:57.800 --> 01:15:59.800
- I write hundreds of e-mails.
- Why didn't you tell me?


01:15:59.700 --> 01:16:02.200
It never occurred to you, in all this time,
that this would be important?


01:16:02.200 --> 01:16:05.100
I didn't make the decision.
I was asked to write a recommendation.


01:16:05.100 --> 01:16:07.900
What was I supposed to do?
Not say my husband knows about this?


01:16:08.000 --> 01:16:10.300
Well, they have this now.


01:16:10.200 --> 01:16:12.900
They'll call me a liar and it will stick.


01:16:12.900 --> 01:16:16.000
'Cause they have all the power.
What do I have? My word.


01:16:16.800 --> 01:16:18.500
You've got to speak up, Valerie.


01:16:18.600 --> 01:16:22.500
You've got to go on the record now.
You've got to defend us. Now.


01:16:24.900 --> 01:16:26.400
So what do you want me to do?


01:16:26.400 --> 01:16:30.100
Go to the papers like you did?
Write a piece in The New York Times?


01:16:30.100 --> 01:16:31.400
You know I'd have to submit it
to the Agency...


01:16:31.400 --> 01:16:32.700
- Daddy!
- Wait, wait, wait.


01:16:32.700 --> 01:16:34.300
Honey, go play. Go on, go on.


01:16:34.400 --> 01:16:35.800
The Agency?


01:16:35.800 --> 01:16:38.900
Valerie, who's your loyalty to?
To your husband or the CIA?


01:16:38.900 --> 01:16:42.200
It's to my family.
I put my family first, always.


01:16:42.200 --> 01:16:45.000
Were you putting them first
when you wrote that goddamn article?


01:16:46.000 --> 01:16:47.300
Mommy!


01:16:47.900 --> 01:16:49.200
Trevor?


01:16:50.100 --> 01:16:51.700
Go find Samantha.


01:16:52.700 --> 01:16:55.800
I'm taking different routes
to and from school.


01:16:55.800 --> 01:17:00.200
I'm looking in empty rooms,
under beds, every time I come home.


01:17:00.000 --> 01:17:01.500
A home we're going to lose pretty soon


01:17:01.500 --> 01:17:04.800
because your work has dried up
and your clients are running for cover.


01:17:04.800 --> 01:17:07.100
What has all this achieved, Joe?


01:17:12.500 --> 01:17:14.200
Maybe you're right.


01:17:15.600 --> 01:17:18.500
Maybe I just should
have kept my mouth shut.


01:17:18.900 --> 01:17:21.800
Is that what your dad taught you, Valerie?


01:17:22.100 --> 01:17:23.800
Is that what Colonel Sam Plame would say?


01:17:23.900 --> 01:17:25.500
A good American
just keeps his mouth shut.


01:17:25.500 --> 01:17:28.300
A good American just looks the other way?


01:17:29.300 --> 01:17:31.300
Did you send me to Niger?


01:17:31.600 --> 01:17:33.800
His business is struggling,
he's on the slide.


01:17:33.800 --> 01:17:36.000
I'll pull a few strings,
send the old man a bone.


01:17:36.000 --> 01:17:38.400
- Is that pretty much what happened?
- How dare you.


01:17:38.400 --> 01:17:40.000
Did you send me?


01:17:40.500 --> 01:17:42.300
You think I'm lying to you.


01:17:42.300 --> 01:17:44.000
Could I tell if you were?


01:17:49.800 --> 01:17:51.400
Trevor? Honey?


01:17:57.500 --> 01:18:00.100
Come on, Sam. Let's get in the car.


01:18:01.100 --> 01:18:03.300
- Bye, guys! I'll see you at home.
- Bye, Daddy!


01:18:03.300 --> 01:18:04.500
Bye!


01:18:04.500 --> 01:18:06.500
I'm taking my car, okay?


01:18:07.800 --> 01:18:10.600
Joe Wilson was a shameless self-promoter.


01:18:10.500 --> 01:18:14.400
Everything about his story was either a lie
or a hoax or he was incompetent.


01:18:14.400 --> 01:18:16.500
I think this is important.
If we're in time of war


01:18:16.500 --> 01:18:17.900
and you want to know
what the President said


01:18:17.900 --> 01:18:19.800
or what the President didn't say,
whether it's accurate or not,


01:18:19.900 --> 01:18:21.400
and you have someone who says,
"I'm sent over there


01:18:21.400 --> 01:18:25.000
"by the Vice President of the United States
and George Tenet to investigate this,"


01:18:25.000 --> 01:18:27.900
and instead it turns out he was sent over
at the recommendation of his wife...


01:18:29.300 --> 01:18:31.300
- There he is!
- Is it him?


01:18:31.900 --> 01:18:33.500
- Mr. Wilson...
- This is private property.


01:18:33.600 --> 01:18:36.500
- You're trespassing.
- Mr. Wilson, did the Vice President...


01:18:36.400 --> 01:18:38.800
Please get off my property!


01:18:38.700 --> 01:18:40.100
- I have no comment!
- Mr. Wilson,


01:18:40.200 --> 01:18:42.000
- was the Niger trip a free holiday?
- Get off the property.


01:18:42.000 --> 01:18:45.100
A boondoggle?
Have you been lying to us from the start?


01:18:45.000 --> 01:18:48.800
I never lied. I didn't receive any payment.
My wife didn't send me. Now, leave.


01:18:48.700 --> 01:18:50.700
- Did the taxpayers pay for your vacation...
- All of you, leave!


01:18:50.700 --> 01:18:52.600
- ...Mr. Wilson?
- It wasn't a vacation.


01:18:52.600 --> 01:18:54.900
It was a fact-finding mission
in the lead-up to a war.


01:18:54.900 --> 01:18:56.100
- What? What?
- Are you against our troops?


01:18:56.200 --> 01:18:57.500
- Get off my property!
- Are you against our troops?


01:18:57.500 --> 01:18:59.000
All the way off the property!


01:18:59.000 --> 01:19:00.200
Mr. Wilson, people are saying


01:19:00.200 --> 01:19:02.200
that your wife doesn't actually work
for the CIA.


01:19:02.200 --> 01:19:04.600
Is it true she's just a secretary?


01:19:04.600 --> 01:19:05.600
Mr. Wilson, is it true that you


01:19:05.700 --> 01:19:06.900
donated money to the Kerry campaign?


01:19:06.800 --> 01:19:08.100
Mr. Wilson, your wife's a nobody!


01:19:08.200 --> 01:19:10.000
Well, I think it's really all about the money.


01:19:10.000 --> 01:19:13.200
We're talking about a third-rate CIA agent


01:19:13.400 --> 01:19:16.000
who had a government salary,
and now she's out.


01:19:16.000 --> 01:19:18.500
She could have transferred somewhere else
within the CIA.


01:19:18.500 --> 01:19:21.400
She didn't have to leave.
Probably the CIA wanted her to leave


01:19:21.400 --> 01:19:24.900
because she had already been in the press
without their permission.


01:19:24.800 --> 01:19:29.200
It's come out that she was considered
kind of a mediocre agent at best.


01:19:46.000 --> 01:19:48.200
Can I just take this pillow?


01:19:55.900 --> 01:20:00.300
When we were at The Farm
training to be field officers,


01:20:02.500 --> 01:20:06.300
they picked out four or five of us
and told us we stood out.


01:20:07.100 --> 01:20:10.600
We were bound, hooded,
thrown into separate cells.


01:20:14.300 --> 01:20:16.300
They deprived us of sleep,


01:20:16.900 --> 01:20:18.100
beat us.


01:20:18.800 --> 01:20:22.500
All we had to do was give up the name
of one of the others.


01:20:23.400 --> 01:20:25.300
Just one name.


01:20:28.100 --> 01:20:31.000
They push you until they find it.


01:20:33.400 --> 01:20:35.300
Until they find the point at which you break.


01:20:37.500 --> 01:20:41.400
And one by one, everybody broke


01:20:42.900 --> 01:20:44.300
except me.


01:20:45.900 --> 01:20:48.200
And that made me feel special.


01:20:50.700 --> 01:20:52.400
You can't break me.


01:20:55.000 --> 01:20:57.500
I don't have a breaking point.


01:21:03.100 --> 01:21:04.500
I was wrong.


01:21:43.900 --> 01:21:46.100
I'm gonna walk down the stairs
because I can't run down them.


01:21:46.100 --> 01:21:49.200
Okay. You go safely,
but, let's go. Quickly.


01:21:49.100 --> 01:21:51.000
Don't forget your jacket. Trevor.


01:21:52.200 --> 01:21:53.800
Okay, say goodbye to your father.


01:21:53.800 --> 01:21:56.900
- Hey, guys.
- We're going on a mystery tour!


01:21:56.800 --> 01:22:01.800
I know you are. Come here. Come here.
I'm going to see you both real soon.


01:22:02.600 --> 01:22:04.500
Why aren't you coming, Daddy?


01:22:04.500 --> 01:22:08.800
- I'm going to see you really soon.
- Okay, let's get in the car, guys.


01:22:09.800 --> 01:22:10.800
You got it?


01:22:18.800 --> 01:22:21.200
Come on, let's go, guys.


01:22:21.500 --> 01:22:22.700
Okay.


01:22:29.300 --> 01:22:31.100
I'm getting soaked!


01:22:45.200 --> 01:22:46.400
- Grandma!
- Grandma.


01:22:46.500 --> 01:22:48.600
- Hi, baby. Hi.
- Hello, Mom.


01:22:48.600 --> 01:22:50.500
Hi, baby, how are you?


01:22:50.500 --> 01:22:54.700
Hey, Trevor, my goodness, how big you are!
Come on in.


01:22:57.000 --> 01:22:59.100
Okay, now do you want
a red one or a green one?


01:22:59.100 --> 01:23:00.500
- Red one!
- Okay.


01:23:00.600 --> 01:23:02.900
- Red one!
- Here's a red one and...


01:23:02.800 --> 01:23:07.500
- Apple?
- Apple and caramels, I think.


01:23:07.500 --> 01:23:09.500
So, what color apple do you want?


01:23:09.400 --> 01:23:10.500
- Red.
- Okay.


01:23:10.500 --> 01:23:13.900
- Green.
- You want a green? Oh, good. I'm glad.


01:23:41.000 --> 01:23:43.000
Afghanistan could quickly revert back to...


01:23:42.900 --> 01:23:45.400
The governments of Niger and Burkina Faso


01:23:45.400 --> 01:23:48.600
are interested in exploiting the
gold reserves along their common border.


01:23:48.900 --> 01:23:51.600
There's not a lot of interest,
as gold's at $150 an ounce.


01:23:55.400 --> 01:23:58.800
But it would compliment your holdings
in East Africa and the concession's cheap.


01:24:01.400 --> 01:24:02.600
My friend.


01:24:05.500 --> 01:24:07.600
- Joe Wilson.
- Karl Moleo Guderron.


01:24:07.600 --> 01:24:08.900
- Such a pleasure.
- Nice to meet you.


01:24:09.000 --> 01:24:10.200
How is your wife, Joe?


01:24:10.400 --> 01:24:12.400
She's fine. She's well. She's...


01:24:12.600 --> 01:24:17.200
Excuse me? Can I just... A black eye,
two shots of espresso, strong coffee.


01:24:17.900 --> 01:24:19.600
I'm not very hungry.


01:24:20.500 --> 01:24:21.700
How long are you in town?


01:24:21.800 --> 01:24:22.800
Just a few days.


01:24:22.800 --> 01:24:25.400
Komolea and I are excited
to hear your proposal.


01:24:33.900 --> 01:24:36.100
Can I help you? Excuse me, can I help you?


01:24:36.100 --> 01:24:38.700
No. I was just telling these men
that you, sir, are a fraud.


01:24:38.700 --> 01:24:39.700
This is a private lunch.


01:24:39.700 --> 01:24:42.300
- Could you leave now, please? Thank you.
- This man is a liar and a traitor.


01:24:42.200 --> 01:24:44.100
- He is in the pay of left-wing hate groups.
- She's just a reporter.


01:24:44.000 --> 01:24:46.200
He's a Democrat stooge
and he's an anti-war zealot.


01:24:46.200 --> 01:24:48.800
- He has stabbed our troops in the back!
- Okay, leave now.


01:24:48.800 --> 01:24:51.100
- Excuse me, I'm very sorry.
- Wilson, you've got blood on your hands


01:24:51.100 --> 01:24:54.000
- and your wife is a traitor and a fantasist.
- Okay, okay, leave my table.


01:24:53.900 --> 01:24:57.200
How dare you talk about my wife.
You don't know her, you don't know me.


01:24:57.300 --> 01:24:59.600
- Now leave now!
- Very nice.


01:24:59.500 --> 01:25:00.800
- You gentlemen should know...
- She's gonna leave.


01:25:00.800 --> 01:25:02.800
- ...you're having lunch with a traitor!
- I think we should leave.


01:25:02.800 --> 01:25:04.100
- Please, don't.
- No, we should.


01:25:04.200 --> 01:25:06.600
- Did you hear the way that this man just...
- Shame on you.


01:25:06.600 --> 01:25:08.000
You call yourself a reporter?


01:25:08.200 --> 01:25:11.100
Shame on you!
You're nothing but a self-promoting hack!


01:25:11.400 --> 01:25:12.500
Bitch.


01:25:20.200 --> 01:25:21.300
Taxi!


01:25:23.500 --> 01:25:25.500
Palisades.


01:25:29.800 --> 01:25:31.900
- You okay?
- I'm fine.


01:25:34.100 --> 01:25:36.600
You're him. I see you on TV.


01:25:36.600 --> 01:25:38.900
- You're Joe Wilson.
- No, I'm not.


01:25:38.900 --> 01:25:42.000
- Yes, brother, I see you on TV.
- That's somebody else.


01:25:41.900 --> 01:25:44.000
No, no, I know you.


01:25:44.000 --> 01:25:47.400
My name is Joe, too.
I'm from Sierra Leone. Freetown.


01:25:47.400 --> 01:25:49.800
You've been there, right?
You like Freetown?


01:25:50.000 --> 01:25:52.600
Joe, you and I both know
Freetown's a shithole.


01:25:52.600 --> 01:25:53.800
That's the truth.


01:25:54.100 --> 01:25:58.400
That's the truth right there, brother.
Yes, indeed, Sierra Leone is dying.


01:25:58.800 --> 01:26:02.000
There's too much injustice
and corruption in Sierra Leone.


01:26:02.000 --> 01:26:05.500
People at the top have too much power,
way too much power.


01:26:05.600 --> 01:26:07.800
But people can't see that from over here.


01:26:07.800 --> 01:26:10.900
Over here, in America, it's a different world.


01:26:11.100 --> 01:26:13.800
- I wouldn't be so sure of that.
- How can you say that?


01:26:13.800 --> 01:26:15.500
Land of the free, brother, home of the brave.


01:26:16.100 --> 01:26:19.900
Joe, could you pull over? I'm just gonna...
Pull over here, I'm gonna walk.


01:26:27.700 --> 01:26:29.300
Keep the change.


01:26:41.600 --> 01:26:43.700
- That's cheating!
- I got it!


01:26:47.800 --> 01:26:48.900
Ready?


01:26:49.100 --> 01:26:52.100
Above your head! Above your head!
Swing your rope!


01:26:52.000 --> 01:26:53.200
How is he?


01:26:53.800 --> 01:26:56.100
He's okay. He's better.


01:26:56.100 --> 01:26:57.800
He's shaking through.


01:27:06.200 --> 01:27:07.700
I win.


01:27:13.200 --> 01:27:14.400
There. There they are.


01:27:14.400 --> 01:27:16.300
Do you see those guys?
Those little yellow fellas?


01:27:16.300 --> 01:27:18.600
- Yeah, I see them.
- See that?


01:27:20.500 --> 01:27:24.100
There's a name for them.
I used to know the name for them.


01:27:24.900 --> 01:27:28.100
Some kind of... They're beautiful.


01:27:38.900 --> 01:27:41.300
I think my marriage is over, Dad.


01:27:54.100 --> 01:27:59.200
I know my little gal doesn't say anything
until she absolutely has to.


01:28:07.300 --> 01:28:10.800
There's going to be
another Congressional Investigation.


01:28:11.200 --> 01:28:14.300
He wants me to speak out.
Go on the record.


01:28:18.200 --> 01:28:21.400
Like that would suddenly make
all of this go away.


01:28:24.100 --> 01:28:26.600
We can't even speak to each other.


01:28:26.700 --> 01:28:29.100
I can remember
saying exactly the same thing.


01:28:29.800 --> 01:28:33.300
July, '72.
Me and your mom weren't getting along,


01:28:33.200 --> 01:28:34.700
we were fighting all the time.


01:28:35.000 --> 01:28:38.600
I guess she just plain had enough
of moving house.


01:28:43.600 --> 01:28:46.400
It wasn't until I retired,
25 years in the Air Force,


01:28:46.300 --> 01:28:48.400
that I realized
that we never did have a home.


01:28:50.400 --> 01:28:54.000
We must have moved 20 different times,
I don't know.


01:28:54.200 --> 01:28:57.400
Germany. Singapore. Australia. England.


01:29:00.800 --> 01:29:04.700
You had 20 different chances
to introduce yourself as someone new.


01:29:05.200 --> 01:29:09.300
You turned out all right, though. Okay.
I mean, you're responsible.


01:29:10.100 --> 01:29:12.200
A little too serious, maybe.


01:29:13.500 --> 01:29:16.500
It made you tough, though, huh?
Real tough.


01:29:18.800 --> 01:29:22.500
Probably tougher than me
and your mom could ever understand.


01:29:24.500 --> 01:29:27.200
I just can't see how this comes around.


01:29:30.200 --> 01:29:31.700
Not this time.


01:29:32.800 --> 01:29:34.100
Not anymore.


01:29:34.400 --> 01:29:37.200
What they did was wrong, Val.
It was just plain wrong.


01:29:37.200 --> 01:29:39.300
Don't you ever forget that.


01:29:40.800 --> 01:29:43.800
You know, say if through some miracle
you get through this thing,


01:29:43.700 --> 01:29:47.000
I mean, there's no guarantee
you and Joe won't fight.


01:29:47.300 --> 01:29:49.200
You know, he's a stubborn son of a bitch.


01:29:49.200 --> 01:29:52.700
I mean, he's not going to give up
any more than you are.


01:29:55.500 --> 01:29:57.000
Grandpa, look.


01:29:58.300 --> 01:30:01.100
I swear to God she's going to
keep at that thing until she licks it.


01:30:01.100 --> 01:30:03.200
Come on, raise your hand up!


01:30:03.200 --> 01:30:04.600
There you go!


01:30:05.400 --> 01:30:08.500
- Good shot.
- I'm going to do it again!


01:30:09.300 --> 01:30:10.400
Yeah.


01:30:11.000 --> 01:30:12.500
Good try!


01:30:16.000 --> 01:30:17.000
...maybe the final results.


01:30:17.100 --> 01:30:18.100
Shit. Mom?


01:30:18.100 --> 01:30:20.600
And it's turned out to be bad news
for one member of the White House team,


01:30:20.600 --> 01:30:23.900
and a central figure he is,
Scooter Libby. Five counts.


01:30:23.900 --> 01:30:27.800
And as Brian Williams just said
on NBC News, in that special report,


01:30:27.700 --> 01:30:29.600
30 years he faces right now.


01:30:29.600 --> 01:30:32.100
And I want to talk right now
to Dan Abrams, my colleague,


01:30:32.000 --> 01:30:33.100
who handles these legal matters...


01:30:33.100 --> 01:30:35.300
You can imagine
that the letter of resignation


01:30:35.200 --> 01:30:38.300
was probably drafted
somewhat in advance


01:30:38.200 --> 01:30:42.100
and that there were indications in the past...


01:30:42.100 --> 01:30:45.400
What is next?
Lawyers for Lewis Scooter Libby


01:30:45.400 --> 01:30:47.600
are preparing his defense
following his indictment on Friday.


01:30:48.600 --> 01:30:51.600
Meanwhile, President Bush
is set to announce his next nominee


01:30:51.600 --> 01:30:55.500
to replace Sandra Day O'Connor
on the Supreme Court.


01:30:55.400 --> 01:30:57.500
Karl Rove escaped indictment today,


01:30:57.500 --> 01:31:01.500
but according to sources
still faces a possible perjury charge.


01:31:01.500 --> 01:31:03.100
Now, two things here.


01:31:03.100 --> 01:31:07.200
First of all,
the Karl Rove business about today,


01:31:07.000 --> 01:31:09.100
the fact that he was not indicted today


01:31:09.100 --> 01:31:12.200
is certainly
what you would call interim good news,


01:31:12.100 --> 01:31:14.300
but it can only be called interim good news


01:31:14.300 --> 01:31:19.900
because as you know, the investigation,
insofar as he is concerned, is going to...


01:31:48.700 --> 01:31:52.300
They served up Scooter Libby.
He's going to take the fall.


01:31:54.900 --> 01:31:56.500
I'm sure they've already brokered a deal.


01:31:56.500 --> 01:32:00.400
He takes the fall, the deck is stacked,
he gets pardoned.


01:32:00.300 --> 01:32:02.700
I bet there won't even be a trial.


01:32:15.200 --> 01:32:19.800
I don't care what they say about us.


01:32:20.600 --> 01:32:23.900
I don't care how angry you get.


01:32:24.300 --> 01:32:27.200
If they take all of this away, I don't care.


01:32:28.200 --> 01:32:32.500
They do not get to take my marriage.


01:32:37.400 --> 01:32:38.500
I'm so sorry.


01:32:40.500 --> 01:32:42.000
You did good.


01:32:43.900 --> 01:32:45.200
I did it for me.


01:32:46.000 --> 01:32:47.900
I know why you did it.


01:32:49.800 --> 01:32:51.100
Thank you.


01:32:57.800 --> 01:33:00.200
If I could give it back to you...


01:33:01.900 --> 01:33:05.500
If I could give you back who you were...


01:33:10.100 --> 01:33:11.700
This is who I am.


01:33:13.500 --> 01:33:14.900
Right here.


01:33:34.400 --> 01:33:36.300
Are you ready to fight?


01:33:40.000 --> 01:33:41.100
Good.


01:33:42.400 --> 01:33:44.000
How many of you know the 16 words


01:33:44.900 --> 01:33:48.500
in President Bush's State of the Union
address that led us to war?


01:33:50.300 --> 01:33:52.800
How many know my wife's name?


01:33:52.800 --> 01:33:54.300
- Valerie Plame.
- Valerie Plame.


01:33:54.300 --> 01:33:58.200
Now, how can you know one
and not the other?


01:33:58.200 --> 01:34:02.700
When did the question move
from "Why are we going to war?"


01:34:03.500 --> 01:34:05.400
to "Who is this man's wife?"


01:34:05.700 --> 01:34:10.200
I asked the first question,
but somebody else asked the second.


01:34:10.200 --> 01:34:11.700
And it worked.


01:34:11.700 --> 01:34:14.100
Because none of us know the truth.


01:34:14.900 --> 01:34:18.700
The offense that was committed
was not committed against me,


01:34:18.600 --> 01:34:21.000
it was not committed against my wife.


01:34:21.000 --> 01:34:23.100
It was committed against you.


01:34:23.400 --> 01:34:25.000
All of you.


01:34:24.900 --> 01:34:28.800
Now, if that makes you angry
or feel misrepresented,


01:34:29.200 --> 01:34:30.800
do something about it.


01:34:31.900 --> 01:34:35.100
When Benjamin Franklin
left Independence Hall


01:34:35.100 --> 01:34:37.200
just after the second drafting,


01:34:37.200 --> 01:34:39.000
he was approached by a woman
on the street.


01:34:39.000 --> 01:34:41.400
The woman said, "Mr. Franklin,


01:34:41.400 --> 01:34:44.700
"what manner of government
have you bequeathed us?"


01:34:44.700 --> 01:34:47.800
And Franklin said, "A Republic, madam.


01:34:48.800 --> 01:34:50.000
"If you can keep it."


01:34:50.400 --> 01:34:53.600
The responsibility of a country


01:34:53.500 --> 01:34:56.900
is not in the hands of a privileged few.


01:34:57.400 --> 01:35:01.300
We are strong, and we are free from tyranny


01:35:01.300 --> 01:35:07.000
as long as each one of us
remembers his or her duty as a citizen.


01:35:06.800 --> 01:35:10.300
Whether it's to report a pothole
at the top of your street


01:35:10.200 --> 01:35:12.400
or lies in a State of the Union address,


01:35:12.400 --> 01:35:15.300
speak out! Ask those questions.


01:35:15.300 --> 01:35:17.000
Demand that truth.


01:35:17.500 --> 01:35:19.900
Democracy is not a free ride, man.


01:35:19.800 --> 01:35:21.700
I'm here to tell you.


01:35:21.700 --> 01:35:24.200
But, this is where we live.


01:35:24.800 --> 01:35:30.000
And if we do our job,
this is where our children will live.


01:35:31.300 --> 01:35:33.000
God bless America.


01:35:38.600 --> 01:35:41.000
Ms. Wilson,
we're pleased to have you here.


01:35:40.900 --> 01:35:44.200
Thank you very much
for coming to our committee today.


01:35:44.100 --> 01:35:48.700
It's the practice of this committee
that all witnesses are administered an oath.


01:35:48.900 --> 01:35:52.000
And I'd like to ask you to stand
and raise your right hand.


01:35:52.400 --> 01:35:55.200
Do you promise to tell the truth
and nothing but the truth?


01:35:55.600 --> 01:35:56.800
- I do.
- Please be seated.


01:36:00.400 --> 01:36:02.200
Now, there's a button
on the base of the mike.


01:36:02.100 --> 01:36:04.800
Be sure to press it in
and pull it closely enough to you


01:36:04.800 --> 01:36:06.700
so you can be heard.


01:36:14.000 --> 01:36:17.500
Good morning, Mr. Chairman
and members of the committee.


01:36:19.000 --> 01:36:21.300
My name is Valerie Plame Wilson.


01:36:23.300 --> 01:36:26.900
And I'm honored to have been invited
to testify under oath


01:36:27.700 --> 01:36:30.700
before the Committee on Oversight
and Government Reform


01:36:30.700 --> 01:36:34.100
on the critical issue
of safeguarding classified information.


01:36:35.200 --> 01:36:39.000
I'm grateful for this opportunity
to set the record straight.


01:36:40.200 --> 01:36:44.100
I served the United States loyally
and to the best of my ability


01:36:44.000 --> 01:36:48.400
as a covert operations officer
for the Central Intelligence Agency.


01:36:49.300 --> 01:36:52.800
I worked on behalf of the national security
of our country,


01:36:52.700 --> 01:36:55.500
on behalf of the people of the United States,


01:36:55.400 --> 01:36:59.800
until my name and true affiliations
were exposed in the national media


01:36:59.800 --> 01:37:04.900
on July 14th, 2003, after a leak
by administration officials.


01:37:05.800 --> 01:37:08.700
Today, I can tell this committee even more.


01:37:09.500 --> 01:37:12.000
In the run-up to the war with Iraq,


01:37:12.000 --> 01:37:15.500
I worked in the counter-proliferation
division of the CIA,


01:37:15.500 --> 01:37:20.400
still as a covert officer whose affiliation
with the CIA was classified.


01:37:21.000 --> 01:37:25.200
I raced to discover solid intelligence
for senior policymakers


01:37:25.200 --> 01:37:28.700
on Iraq's presumed weapons
of mass destruction programs.


01:37:29.300 --> 01:37:33.300
While I helped to manage
and run secret world-wide operations


01:37:33.100 --> 01:37:37.900
against this WMD target
from CIA headquarters in Washington,


01:37:37.700 --> 01:37:43.000
I also traveled to foreign countries
on secret missions


01:37:42.900 --> 01:37:45.000
to find vital intelligence.


01:37:45.500 --> 01:37:48.600
I loved my career
because I love my country.


01:37:48.600 --> 01:37:51.000
I was proud of the serious responsibilities


01:37:51.100 --> 01:37:54.700
entrusted to me
as a CIA covert operations officer.

